\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Justified -  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Governor\b0\par\par\uc2 151 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2010\par 19:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1810 GMT [Dow Jones] Despite the strength the Chilean peso, current conditions don't justify \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market,\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio told Chile's Senate. The peso has been trading most of the fourth quarter at around 31-month highs against the dollar, which exporters claim is cutting the competitiveness of their products abroad. De Gregorio said that while \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  couldn't be ruled out, it is an expensive and not always useful tool to weaken the exchange rate. He added that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market could have negative consequences on the economy and could fuel capital inflows that would be counterproductive to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (carolina.pica@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (robert.flint@dowjones.com) \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Robert Flint, 212-416-2216; \par robert.flint@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 14-12-10 1810GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101214e6ce001e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
