\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firm on China, US tax deal\b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2010\par 14:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil real adds 0.82 pct, Mexico peso up 0.47 pct\par \par \uc2 * Record copper price lifts Chile peso to 30-month high\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso lifted by U.S. tax cut extension deal (Recasts; adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Dec 13 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed on Monday after China held back from raising interest rates over the weekend, easing concerns that one of the region's top trading partners could put the brakes on growth.\par \par \uc2 Global equity markets rose and the dollar broadly weakened after China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended an increase in reserve requirements for top banks rather than raise benchmark interest rates. For details, see [ID:nL3E6ND0F6]\par \par \uc2 Some had feared China could hike interest rates, which could slow growth and curb demand for Latin American commodities such as Chilean copper and Brazil's iron ore.\par \par \uc2 "The climate in global markets has improved. The majority of stock markets are up and this is also an indication of risk appetite. Because of this the real is stronger," said Reginaldo Galhardo, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at the Treviso brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pierced the closely-watched level of 1.70 per dollar and last bid 0.82 percent stronger at 1.699 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 Some think the level could spur the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to keep the real's strength from hurting local companies, whose exports are becoming more expensive abroad as they compete with cheapening imports.\par \par \uc2 "The hanging sword of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very much alive in the country, and investors must not downplay this risk," analysts at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  wrote in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Traders across the region noted that volume was dropping as most clients were winding down business ahead of the holiday season.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has tripled a tax on capital inflows into local bonds and regularly bought dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent months to curb the real's rally.\par \par \uc2 TAX RELIEF RALLY\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> strengthened 0.47 percent to 12.3917 per dollar, helped by signs that U.S. President Barack Obama's tax deal with Republicans to extend cuts will likely win grudging passage in the Congress. [ID:nN12152826]\par \par \uc2 Some think the tax cut extension could help fuel growth next year in the United States, Mexico's top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 "The market is seeing this as good for the economy," said Roberto Melzi, a strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> hit a fresh 30-month high early on Monday, but later pared some gains to trade 0.25 percent stronger at 474.8 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso was boosted by the price of copper, which hit a new high after China's decision to eschew an interest rate hike lifted optimism about demand for the red metal.\par \par \uc2 Unlike Brazilian authorities, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  has held back from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in financial markets.\par \par \uc2 "All the fundamentals keep playing in favor of the peso, with markets mostly positive, the price of copper again hit a record prices and the dollar is weak around the globe," said a trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101216e6cd000wp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
