\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Chile Inflation To End 2010 At 3% - \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Governor\b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2010\par 13:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 10 Dec 2010 07:55 EDT *DJ  Chilean Peso In Line With Fundamentals -\b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor\par \par \uc2 10 Dec 2010 08:01 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile Forex Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Available If Needed-\b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor\par \par \uc2 10 Dec 2010 08:02 EDT *DJ  Firm Chile Peso Has Moderated Rate Hikes-\b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor\par \par \uc2 10 Dec 2010 08:25 EDT DJ  Chile Inflation To End 2010 At 3% - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Inflation in Chile will likely end this year at 3% as inflationary pressures have subsided, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rodrigo Vergara said Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently expects inflation to end at 3.9% in 2010, but that outlook will likely be revised to 3% when it releases its quarterly Monetary Policy Report later this month.\par \par \uc2 A strong peso in relation to the dollar has contributed to easing inflationary pressures as imports have become cheaper. In recent months, the peso has been trading at around 31-month highs against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Vergara, in prepared remarks delivered at a seminar, said the peso's strength had moderated the pace at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is withdrawing its significant monetary stimulus.\par \par \uc2 After holding the benchmark overnight rate at a record low 0.5% since July 2009, in June 2010 the bank began increase the rate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially began increasing the rate at a pace of 50 basis points a month, but decelerated this pace at its October meeting, when it only increased the benchmark rate a quarter of a percentage point.\par \par \uc2 In November, it increased the rate another 25 basis points to 3.0%, but according to the minutes of that meeting, it considered taking a temporary pause amid reduced inflationary pressures and a strong peso.\par \par \uc2 Higher local interest rates put pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to post further gains, which is damaging to the country's export sector. Chile is highly dependent on its exports, especially of natural resources such as copper, fertilizers, wood pulp, fresh fruits and wines.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Anthony Esposito contributed to this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 10, 2010 08:25 ET (13:25 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020101210e6ca002yr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
