\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Likely Not Imminent To Dismay Of Exporters\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 656 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2010\par 20:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Despite Chilean exporters' pleas for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the peso hovers near a 30-month high versus the dollar, a move by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in that direction likely isn't imminent.\par \par \uc2 As the U.S. economy limps along and the U.S. Federal Reserve pursues aggressive monetary easing, the dollar has swooned as investors seek better returns in emerging markets, including Chile.\par \par \uc2 The Andean nation's peso has also gained as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightens monetary conditions, investments pour in as part of recovery efforts from a devastating February earthquake and as international copper prices shoot higher.\par \par \uc2 Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, so repatriated receipts from copper sales abroad have a major influence on the peso.\par \par \uc2 In response to the peso's appreciation, which reduces exporters' competitiveness overseas, Chile's government cut red tape for their products and state-owned bank BancoEstado will offer up to a $200 million dollar-denominated credit line to small and medium-size companies.\par \par \uc2 Exporters, however, contend that more can be done to combat the peso's strength. "Those measures just aren't enough because the exchange rate weighs so much on the ability to remain competitive in this business," said Antonio Walker, president of the Fedefruta fruit exporters trade group.\par \par \uc2 Over the last decade, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market three times, and the last time it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in April 2008, the peso was trading at 10-year highs against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 When the peso was trading at CLP488.90 to the dollar in late October, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio said, "if an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were justified today, we'd already be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," although he added then that an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was more likely than it had been even three months ago. The peso closed at CLP483.40 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has room to increase its international reserves by around $5 billion to $8 billion, which would push the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down by about CLP20, said Sergio Tricio, head of studies with local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile.\par \par \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  senior emerging-markets analyst Eduardo Suarez argues, however, that Chile's push to become a regional financial hub and its intention to make the peso a deliverable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 --so it can be bought and sold everywhere--will lead the government to seek more market-friendly measures that decrease the likelihood of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Exporters, though, are pointing to other countries, such as Brazil, that have implemented measures to stanch their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' growth. Brazil last month raised its financial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  tax on fixed-income securities and some equities, while its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is purchasing dollars.\par \par \uc2 "The fact is the Chilean peso ... has not appreciated as much as (the Brazilian real), hence it does give Chile some room to maneuver for now," Standard Chartered Bank's Mike Moran said.\par \par \uc2 If the peso breaks the CLP475 barrier and gains to levels around CLP450-CLP460, traders see an increased risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although traders argue that a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would in all likelihood have only a transitory effect as copper prices remain high, interest-rate differences continue to make Chile an attractive market and the dollar remains soft internationally, exporters say a short-term reprieve from the peso's strength would be welcome.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 17-11-10 1934GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101117e6bh0014q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
