\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Unlikely -Investment Bank\b0\par\par\uc2 1,178 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2010\par 14:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1357 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the domestic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to weaken the strong peso, according to local investment bank Banchile Inversiones. The peso, in real terms, is trading in line with long-term fundamentals and its strength stems from international, not local factors. "Given these factors, we believe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't the likiest scenario, at least in the near term," Banchile said. (carolina.pica@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1355 GMT [Dow Jones] The spread between the 30-year yield and the 10-year yield rose earlier in the session to a record high of 155.8 basis points as the spread's quarterly chart shows. See chart at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4889"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4889}}}\par \par \uc2 A widening beyond the record level would take the spread up to 168.7BP.\par \par \uc2 But charts suggest that a narrowing below 146.1BP would be the signal for a dip 129.2BP. In that case take profit at 138.6BP.(stephen.cox@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1349 GMT [Dow Jones] Emerging market bonds are stronger with U.S. stocks after the Fed voted for a second round of quantitative easing, spurring more investors to exit the U.S. dollar and chase higher yields in the faster growing emerging markets. The risk premium on \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's Emerging Markets Bond Index Global is 4 bps tighter to 270ps over Tsys. The index is up 0.46. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1341 GMT [Dow Jones] Mid-2012 rate hike odds fall in fed-funds futures on the day after FOMC imposed QE2 and as weekly jobless claims climb. July 2012 contract recently priced in 50% chance for FOMC to raise funds rate to 0.5% in late June 2012 FOMC meeting. That's down from 60% chance Wed. Shorter-dated May '12 prices in 38% chance for 0.5% rate after late Apr FOMC meeting. That's down from 42% chance Wed. Volume in these contracts a little higher compared to recent days. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1339 GMT [Dow Jones] Fed chairman Bernanke is in today's Washington Post laying out the arguments for Fed's QE2. He writes "This approach eased financial conditions in the past and, so far, looks to be effective again." That's mosly through lower rates spurring borrowing and higher stock prices helping household wealth and--hopefully--spending. He holds open door for fine-tuning policy: "We will review the purchase program regularly to ensure it is working as intended and to assess whether adjustments are needed as economic conditions change," he writes. (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1328 GMT [Dow Jones] Large move in the belly of the Tsy curve has pushed super premium (4.5%- 5.5% coupons) mortgage-backed securities up considerably. "It's silly," trader says, "The street is short and some leveraged money market accounts are pushing them." While this sector provides a nice yield kicker over Treasurys, at a premium of 105-108, the writedown is quite costly should prepayments unexpectedly kick up. The GSEs have already pulled all the delinquent loans out of these pools, so prepays would have to come from real homeowners. When the "low rates for very, very long" hits the local papers, some of these folks may decide the hassle factor is worth a refi. After all, these are loans from 5%- 6%. (darlene.ross@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1334 GMT [Dow Jones] Investors are already demanding a record high premium to own the 30-yr Treasury instead of 10-yr note. But strategists at CRT Capital say they "very much think 30s will underperform and have argued for 10s/30s to 165-175 bp" compared to 155.3 BP trading recently. But the strategists question whether the widening gap tells us "about inflation expectations really or rather simply the Fed's effort to make us believe in inflation expectations." (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1325 GMT [Dow Jones] Continued leap in Eurodollar futures prices means the market believes QE2 will keep short-term rates low for a very long period. It's also the result of sharper-than-expected increase in weekly jobless claims. Quarterly 2012 contracts recently up 1.5 to 4.5 BP. 2013 contracts recently 6.5 to 10.5 BP higher. Nearest 1-yr calendar spread tighter, as Dec 2011 contract prices in a rate only 19 BP above rate priced into Dec '10. Same spread at 22 BP Wed. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1319 GMT[Dow Jones] As investors await what EBCB's Trichet has to say at 9:30am ET about backing away from bank's stimulus measures, EUR/USD continues to surge. Hits $1.4253, up from 1.4122 from late Wed, according to EBS via CQG. "Some of the rationale behind the reversal [from lows in June] is that the ECB is today running its policies in the opposite direction to those at the Fed," explaining the rise, says Andrew Wilkinson of Interactive Brokers.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1313 GMT [Dow Jones] Worries have abounded that municipalities have over borrowed and could be the source of the next market meltdown. But "these warnings demonstrate a fundmental misunderstanding of municipal finance," say Bernstein Global Wealth Mgmt analysts. The amount of outstanding muni debt has grown overall, but growth has been in line with that of personal income. Also, debt service also represents just 5% of the largest states' budgets on avg, a manageable figure, Bernstein says. Munis also tend to issue debt for infrastructure, with debt generally maturing in even chunks at regular intervals, so "unlike Greece, municipal issuers are not faced with a wave of debt requiring refinancing," Bernstein says. (kelly.nolan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1313 GMT [Dow Jones] Greece/10-year bund spread rises 22bps since their open on Thursday to stand at 866bps as political instability persists. Turnover is moderate at EUR90M on the local HDAT and European trading platforms. "The widening trend is continuing and I don't expect it to reverse itself unless this Sunday's elections are put behind us and the threat of destabilizing early national polls is lifted," says a senior local bond trader. (nick.skrekas@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1311 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Coca Cola Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Chemical\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Electric Capital Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and Oglethorpe Power are all in the market to sell bonds following the Fed's decision to pump $600B of liquidity into the system and bring Treasury rates even lower. The majority of notes are between 5- and 10-years, where the Fed purchasing is expected to be focused, but Oglethorpe's deal is a 30-year where the yield is expected to rise because of less Fed support in that part of the curve. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Coca Cola\f28 \uc2 \f2 's bonds could smash the record low coupons on 3- and 5- year debt, according to one syndicate manager.(katy.burne@dowjones.com) [ 11-04-10 0959ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101104e6b40009u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
