\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Head:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Yet Merited\b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2010\par 15:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (updates with additional comment from the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--If the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  merited an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio told Friday's Diario Financiero newspaper.\par \par \uc2 With the peso trading at around 29-month highs against the dollar, exporters who've lost competitiveness abroad have called for market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were justified today, we'd already be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," De Gregorio told the newspaper.\par \par \uc2 He noted, however, that an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more likely now than it was three months ago, "because the exchange rate in real terms has appreciated and the occurrence of more complex phenomena can't be ruled out."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monitors the peso's real, not nominal, exchange rate, which factors in inflation, trade flows and other parameters.\par \par \uc2 Agricultural sector exporters have been the hardest hit by the peso's appreciation, especially as the southern hemisphere summer harvest season is about to begin.\par \par \uc2 The central banker said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  couldn't make decisions based on sectorial problems, such as those the agricultural sector faces.\par \par \uc2 "For sectorial problems, you have to use sectorial tools; when the problems are aggregated, the decisions must be macroeconomic," he said, noting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't make sectorial decisions.\par \par \uc2 He told the newspaper the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have a steadfast rule regarding when to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We don't follow a dogma regarding free-floating or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because the latter isn't always the solution each time the peso strengthens," he said.\par \par \uc2 In the past 10 years, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in three instances.\par \par \uc2 Regarding capital controls, De Gregorio said the reserve requirement on foreign investment Chile applied in the 1990s is no longer a solution to be used.\par \par \uc2 "We don't have a massive net inflow of capital, and we have a small current account deficit for this year," he said.\par \par \uc2 He added that should there be a massive inflow as a result of high interest rates, then the bank could implement some sort of capital control.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 29-10-10 1300GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101029e6at001vf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
