\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Watching Peso, Can't Rule Out  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2010\par 20:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "closely monitoring" the appreciating peso and can't rule out future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Enrique Marshall said Monday, according to local newswire Valor Futuro.\par \par \uc2 With the peso recently trading near 29-month highs, exporters have demanded the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, arguing that the peso's strength eats away at the competitiveness of their products.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's job is to provide stable monetary and financial conditions. Regarding the exchange rate, there's been a considerable appreciation of the peso, which we monitor closely, because it impacts economic activity, for instance inflation," Marshall was quoted as saying at a seminar in the northern mining hub Antofagasta.\par \par \uc2 Marshall added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Over the last decade, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market three times, and the last time it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in April 2008, the peso was trading at 10-year highs against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended stronger at CLP486.20 to the dollar Monday, versus Friday's close of CLP486.90.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 25-10-10 1806GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101025e6ap001ef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
