\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Firmer After G-20; Moderated By  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Comment\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2010\par 19:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended mildly stronger against the dollar Monday, as major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the euro, gained sharply on the greenback after the Group of 20 nations agreed over the weekend to avoid "competitive devaluation" of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and as international copper prices firmed.\par \par \uc2 The peso's gains, however, were mitigated by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments that it couldn't rule out an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the peso continues to firm.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at CLP486.20 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP486.90, while trading in a range of CLP483.90 to CLP486.60.\par \par \uc2 The nonbinding agreement among the G-20 nations freed investors from the fear of governments actively pushing their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower and spurred more dollar selling.\par \par \uc2 As Europe is one of Chile's main trade partners, the peso often moves in the same direction as the euro does against the dollar. In recent trading, the euro posted strong gains on the dollar, and the ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traded at lows last seen in January--at 76.962 from 77.494.\par \par \uc2 Also, as Chile is the world's premier copper producer, accounting for a third of global supply, the peso often takes cues from the metal's international prices. Copper traded at its highest since July 2008 in London, as the weak U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fueled investment across the commodities sector.\par \par \uc2 With the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterating that it can't rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though, the peso's gains were limited.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the few cases, along with advanced nations, where the [\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market] hasn't been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  or capital controls haven't been applied, although they're tools that we can't rule out may be used," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio said earlier Monday at a seminar for agricultural businessmen.\par \par \uc2 With the peso recently trading at 29-month highs versus the dollar, exporters, particularly the agricultural sector, have clamored for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the strength of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cuts into the competitiveness of their products.\par \par \uc2 "Continued verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has investors a bit uneasy and they don't want to be caught by surprise. That's what has been keeping the peso trading in a tight range recently," said Eduardo Kutscher, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader for local investment bank Celfin Capital.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as participants awaited a scheduled auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign bonds, as well as local shopping center operator Mall Plaza's issue of $220 million in five-year and 21-year inflation-indexed bonds.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.72%, from 2.70% on Friday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 3.10%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 25-10-10 1722GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101025e6ap001e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
