\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: MGM To Refinance More Bank Debt With $500M Notes\b0\par\par\uc2 1,115 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2010\par 16:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1415 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 MGM Resorts International\f28 \uc2 \f2  (MGM) is offering $500 mln of senior unsecured notes due 2016 via lead underwriter \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Proceeds will repay part of the $1.2 billion of its senior credit facility due to mature in October 2011. In February, lenders representing $4.37 billion of the $5.55 billion senior bank credit facility agreed to extend the maturity of their portion to 2014 from 2011. Notes expected to price later Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (michael.aneiro@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1414 GMT [Dow Jones] Better-than-expected new home sales report does little to alter bullish sentiment of higher prices/lower yields in U.S. interest rate futures. Eurodollar futures prices stay higher, with quarterly 2011 through 2013 contracts recently up 2 to 5 BP. Long-term Tsy futures don't stray far from session highs, with Dec 10-yr Tsy notes recently at 126-29, from 126-30+ session high. Dec 30-yr Tsy bonds recently up a point at 132-22, from 132-132-26 session high. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1410 GMT [Dow Jones] With speculation focused on QE2, fed-funds futures rule out funds rate increase for all of next year. Jan 2012 contract sees 0% chance for FOMC to raise funds rate to 0.5% by end of next year, from 4% chance Fri. Same contract priced in 48% chance on Oct. 1. Volume very light in th Jan '12 contract. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1412 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds rise Monday, supported by gains in Treasurys on expectations that the Fed will announce another round of asset purchases in November. The St Louis Fed's Research Director Christopher Weller says the likelihood of the FOMC announcing additional asset purchases at next week's meeting is pretty high, adding that an approach under discussion is to buy as much as $250Bln between meetings. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in a research note, says purchases could total $2Tln. The front-end the curve outperforms Monday, reversing some of the curve flattening witnessed in recent sessions. The 3-month Euribor Monday fixed at its highest rate since early July, although Eonia fixed lower on Friday. Given the bullish undertone, the market also ignored a faster than expected rise in euro zone industrial production in August. December bunds are up 0.21 at 129.86 and the 10-year bund is higher at 98.24, yielding 2.408%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1409 GMT [Dow Jones] After better-than-expected Sept existing home sales, EUR/USD declines to 1.4018, but still up from 1.3923 late Fri, according to EBS via CQG. USD/JPY moves to 80.55 from 81.41 from late Fri - further away from 15-yr low hit overnight.(andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1409 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish bond prices strengthen on the shorter end of the curve, while 10-year bonds weaken, in very thin trade, "from which no deep conclusions can be drawn" as investors are in position ahead of Poland's monthly monetary policy council meeting on Wednesday, a dealer says. "Everyone has placed their bets on whether the council will raise rates or not," he says. "If a rate increase does occur, bond prices are likely to weaken." Average yield on 2-year bonds is at 4.72% from 4.74% late Friday, 5-year flat at 5.18% from 5.20%, 10-year at 5.61% from 5.59%. EUR/PLN trades at 3.9249 from 3.9691 late Friday; USD/PLN at 2.7990 from 2.8459. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1408 GMT [Dow Jones] Despite 10.0% pop in sales, the number of homes for sales remains very high. Inventories of used homes decreased by 1.9% at the end of September to 4.04 million, but that represented a still hefty 10.7-month supply at the current sales pace. With so much supply, prices are still under pressure. The median price for an existing home was $171,700 in September. That's down 2.4% from $175,900 in September 2009.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1406 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasury prices remain up despite much better than expected rise in existing home sales, as participants remain focused on more QE. Talk in the market that new QE program could total a massive $2T. Investors tuned into Fed remarks today, with Dudley, Bullard and Hoenig to speak. 10-yr up 16/32 to 2.504%, 2-yr flat to 0.351%. (deborah.blumberg@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1403 GMT [Dow Jones] The post-credit housing market is recovering faster than expected. Sales of existing homes increased by 10.0% to an annual rate of 4.53 million. Economists had expected existing home sales to rise only 5.3% to 4.35 million. The increase in resales was the second in a row. In August, resales rose 7.3% to a rate of 4.12 million, revised down from an originally reported 7.6% increase to a 4.13 million rate. (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1401 GMT [Dow Jones] Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may allow the ruble to appreciate in order to keep a lid on inflation, \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. Prices for oil - Russia's chief export - will be driven higher by a low interest rate environment and capital inflows into emerging markets, the investment bank adds. Ruble +1% versus dollar at 35.22. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1358 GMT [Dow Jones] The 10-yr yield broke down on the hourly chart a week ago when it fell below 2.521% channel support. See chart at\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4816"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4816}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 It's targeting 2.464% support. But a recovery above 2.521% would, instead, be the signal for a test of 2.565% resistance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (stephen.cox@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1355 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's peso gains against the dollar following a pledge from G-20 finance ministers to refrain from "competitive devaluation" of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , clearing the road for more greenback sales. With the dollar falling broadly against its major rivals, international copper prices --a key reference for the peso-- shot up to a 27 month high in London trading. Amid peso appreciation, recently at 29-month highs, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has said it can't rule out \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to strengthen. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peso recently stronger at CLP484.50 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP486.90. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com) [ 10-25-10 1015ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101025e6ap0008x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
