\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: After G-20, Chile Peso Continues Firming\b0\par\par\uc2 1,151 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2010\par 15:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1355 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's peso gains against the dollar following a pledge from G-20 finance ministers to refrain from "competitive devaluation" of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , clearing the road for more greenback sales. With the dollar falling broadly against its major rivals, international copper prices --a key reference for the peso-- shot up to a 27 month high in London trading. Amid peso appreciation, recently at 29-month highs, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has said it can't rule out \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to strengthen. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peso recently stronger at CLP484.50 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP486.90. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1353 GMT [Dow Jones] While US data has been better of late, it seems unlikley that anything new before Fed's Nov 2 meeting will be enough to push Fed away from a return to QE, say analysts. Assumptions on data before Nov is that while it may be better - it will not be good enough to avoid more stimulus. "Even as improved activity data further diminishes double-dip fears, we expect price data to keep QE expectations well entrenched," say \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  analysts. Sept existing home sales due at 10am ET. EUR/USD at 1.4022 from 1.3923 late Fri, according to EBS via CQG. USD/JPY at 80.55 from 81.41.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1339 GMT [Dow Jones] National Rural Utilities (A1/A+) is selling collateral trust bonds, (if Natl Rural were to default on the bonds, the holders would receive the securities held in trust). The $500M issue will include 3- and 5-yr pieces and will be sold via active bookrunners BofAML/JPM/Mizuho. (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1338 GMT [Dow Jones] It's a "challenging week for municipal bonds as supply should top" $11B, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Miller Tabak\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Michael Pietronico in a tweet. Taxable Build America bonds are the largest offerings this week, says Janney Montgomery analysts. New York City Transitional Finance Authority is selling $620M of BABs. Increased sales of BABs are expected as the program is set to expire at the end of the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (romy.varghese@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1327 GMT [Dow Jones] Eurodollar futures prices perched at or near session highs even as stocks set to open higher. Talk of aggressive QE2 talk resurfaces even though St. Louis Fed president Bullard suggested last week that Fed Tsy buys would be done in "small increments." Quarterly 2011 through 2012 contracts recently up 1.5 to 3.5 BP. 2013 contracts 4 to 5 BP higher. Smaller gain for nearby Dec 2010 contact as it's more closely aligned to 3-month dollar Libor, which was unchanged Mon at 0.28844%. Dec '10 recently up 1 BP at 99.67, seeing 0.33% Libor at Dec. 13 contract expiration. That's down from 0.34% projected Libor at Fri's settlement. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1324 GMT [Dow Jones] Pumped up imports and rising profit remittances mean Brazil is heading for a record current account deficit in 2011 of $70 billion, according to Banco Safra economists in a research note. A strong Brazilian real makes imports more attractive while a booming economy will lead to hefty profits for multinationals, Safra says. The bank estimates Brazil's 2010 current account deficit at $48.5 billion. (tom.murphy@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1310 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sonoco Products\f28 \uc2 \f2  (Baa3/BBB+), manufacturer of consumer and industrial packaging, is selling $300M of 30-year sr unsecured bonds via active bookrunners BofAML/WFS in order to purchase its outstanding notes due 2013, 2016 and 2021. The offering will include a change of control option at a price of 101. Pricing is expected later this session. (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1304 GMT [Dow Jones] Long-term Tsy futures prices sharply higher, with 30-yr Tsy bond contracts up a little more than a point, as market seems more optimistic that QE2 will involve masssive amounts of Fed Tsy buys. Also, this week's Tsy auctions are not concentrated on long-end, bolstering curve flattening trades. Dec 30-yr Tsy bonds recently reached 132-26, with resistance at last Wed's high for the week at 132-30. Further upside to 133-08 reduces 30-yr cash yield equivalent to 3.875%, says Optima Investment Research. Dec 10-yr Tsy notes recently hit session high of 126-30+, targeting resistance at last Wed's high for the week at 127-07, dropping 10-yr cash yield equivalent below 2.5%. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1252 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Business Media\f28 \uc2 \f2  (Baa3/BBB-) is in the market with a benchmark-sized offering of 10-year bonds via joint lead managers \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 /\f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2 /\f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 /JPM. The issue is expected to be sold this week in the private placement Rule 144a market. (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1251 GMT [Dow Jones] Dollar weakness is pointing the euro, at $1.4016, to the $1.4285-$1.4329 resistance band. Initial daily support is $1.3857.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dollar Index, at 76.951, is near daily support at 76.114. Resistance is 77.645.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar, which is trading at Y80.66, is targeting the April 1995 low of 79.75.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (stephen.cox@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1248 GMT [Dow Jones] It could be feast or famine this week in the high-grade corporate bond market. While the focus will be on earnings and housing data, it's also the last full week before the US election and the next FOMC meeting so there will be considerable focus on election polls and QE, according to analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 JP Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Still, the ridiculously low cost of financing might prompt debt offerings. Additionally, this weekend's IMF meeting concluded with no substantive language on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy coordination going forward. "To the extent this is bad for the dollar it is generally bullish for US corporate earnings and credit metrics," they said. (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1244 GMT [Dow Jones] 5-year CDS written on \f28 \uc2 \f2 LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton\f28 \uc2 \f2  (MC.FR) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Diageo\f28 \uc2 \f2  (DGE.LN) are among the iTraxx Europe constituents underperforming the index Monday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 LVMH\f28 \uc2 \f2  is 1bp wider at 94/98bps and Diago is 0.5bps wider at 72.25/76.75bps, according to Markit, while Europe is 2.25bps tighter at 96bps. \f28 \uc2 \f2 LVMH\f28 \uc2 \f2  said over the weekend that it holds 14.2% of the share capital of Hermes, although it doesn't intend to take control of the firm. However, if it did, analysts reckon one way to raise funds would be to sell the remainder of its Moet Hennessy drinks unit to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Diageo\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which already owns a stake in the unit. (mark.brown@dowjones.com) [ 10-25-10 0958ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101025e6ap0008d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
