\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Chile acts to help exporters hit by strong peso\b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2010\par 17:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Finmin says measure key to control \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  effects\par \par \uc2 * Market says measure weak, not see immediate impact\par \par \uc2 * Gov't to continue analyzing other measures\par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comment and background)\par \par \uc2 By Felipe Iturrieta and Alonso Soto\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Oct 21 (Reuters) - Chile will cut red tape on customs to help exporters hit by a strong peso as one measure to ease the effects of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rapid appreciation, Finance Minister Felipe Larrain said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "This was one of the main measures that we had planned for this week because this is a measure that takes into consideration the exchange rate problem that we are facing," Larrain told reporters at a customs office in the outskirts of Santiago. "This is not the last measure, we will keep analyzing alternatives."\par \par \uc2 Larrain said the move, which was not as strong as many analysts expected, added to tight control over fiscal spending, use of copper savings and offering dollar credits to help exporters whose profits have dwindled because of the stronger peso.\par \par \uc2 "This sort of announcement has no effect," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader in Santiago. "What the market was awaiting for was concrete measures. This was no good, and that's why the the dollar fell again."\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=CL> on Thursday pared some early losses triggered by the government announcement of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures. The peso was 0.19 percent weaker at 485.30/485.80 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ For a TAKE A LOOK on Chile's economy, peso [ID:nN30113748] For SCENARIOS on possible Chile \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves [ID:nN20224723] \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  For a Latam \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  graphic, see   \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/qaq49p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/qaq49p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  For a Chile \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  graphic, see   \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/raq49p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/raq49p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  FACTBOX on steps to counter hot money        [ID:nSGE69503F]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chile has not yet followed the steps of other Latin American countries that have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to temper their local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which are rapidly appreciating on the back of greater capital inflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors chasing high interest rates provided by fast-growing emerging economies have swamped these countries with dollars, pushing up the value of local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chile's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also allayed market talk of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the short-term.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's different approach is sure to attract attention. If this does help exporters ride things out until the peso loses some power, then others could follow suit," said IGM-EMERG in a note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tensions over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and economic imbalances have already surfaced one day before a gathering of finance ministers from the Group of 20 rich and emerging nations gather in South Korea. [ID:nN21252058]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil, which has raised taxes on local bond purchases by foreigners twice this month to rein in the real, on Thursday urged the United States to make the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issue a top priority at the G20 meeting. [ID:nN21289476]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chilean peso has strengthened around 12 percent against the dollar since the end of June, prompting demands for action by exporters hit by rising costs. (Reporting by Felipe Iturrieta and Alonso Soto; Editing by Andrew Hay and Padraic Cassidy)\f28 \par \par \uc2 CHILE-LARRAIN/PESO (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|U|RBN|M|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101021e6al001h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
