\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real extends rally against Chilean peso\b0\par\par\uc2 794 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2010\par 16:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Traders brush off recent attempt to slow real's gains\par \par \uc2 * Mexico and Brazil launch new bond sales\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real firms 0.8 pct, Mexican peso jumps 0.9 pct\par \par \uc2 * Colombia and \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  prepare for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices to afternoon)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Froilan Romero\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Oct 20 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real hit a two-month high against the Chilean peso on Wednesday, as efforts by both countries to curb damaging rallies in their local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  evoked different reactions from traders.\par \par \uc2 A broadly weak dollar provided support to Latin America's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday due to increasing speculation that the Federal Reserve will print more money to boost the struggling U.S. economy. An influential report gave investors clues on Wednesday about how big the stimulus package could be, a source told Reuters [ID:nN20129482]\par \par \uc2 But that support hasn't been felt equally across the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, in part due to the different approaches that individual governments are taking to slow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.\par \par \uc2 A strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes exports more expensive and difficult to sell, potentially endangering long-term growth.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real gained as much as 1.1 percent against the Chilean peso <BRLCLP=R> on Wednesday -- its strongest level against the Andean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Aug. 10 according to the international reference rate.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has taken aggressive action to curb a recent rally in the real, which is now the world's most overvalued major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought more dollars in the market, while the government has increased its tax on foreign purchases of bonds, which it raised again on Monday. But investors have largely brushed off the measures. That is due to Brazil's compelling economic fundamentals, including a high benchmark interest rate widely expected to be held at 10.75 percent at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's meeting later on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva said on Wednesday the government will take as many measures as necessary to curb the real's rally. [ID:nSAQ002514]\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, mere hints at possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Felipe Larrain on Tuesday were enough to keep traders nervous. [ID:nN19122042]\par \par \uc2 "Up until now investors have largely assumed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but in Brazil there has been a certain expectation built in that they would continue to introduce more measures and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively," said Nick Chamie of \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "That mind shift is now slowly being priced in so that's why you're seeing a heightened sense of sensitivity to any mention of it."\par \par \uc2 BONDS BONANZA\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have enjoyed a multi-week rally as traders have bet that U.S. stimulus measures will keep yields on U.S. Treasuries near to record lows, encouraging more investors to buy the region's higher-yielding debt.\par \par \uc2 That trend was briefly interrupted on Tuesday due to a surprise interest rate increase from China, which boosted the dollar and caused sharp losses among the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the dollar resumed its decline on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 After losing more than 1 percent on Tuesday, the real strengthened 0.77 percent to 1.672 on the local spot market <BRBY>, not far from a two-year high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> firmed 0.91 percent to 12.4122 per dollar -- more than 6 percent stronger than it was at the beginning of September.\par \par \uc2 Both countries also moved to take advantage of this frenzied demand for their debt.\par \par \uc2 Brazil said it plans to sell more of its 2028 global bonds denominated in reais, while Mexico sold 150 billion yen ($1.84 billion) of Samurai bonds, IFR reported. [ID:nTOE69J013] and [ID:nSPG003094].\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=> gained 0.54 percent to 484.40 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The market is on tenterhooks, waiting for possible measures by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the peso from continuing to appreciate," said one trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 Dollar purchases would be the most likely way of curbing the rally in the peso, which is trading around a 29-month high against the dollar, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso <COP=RR>, which has surged around 12 percent against the dollar so far this year, was only 0.4 percent stronger on Wednesday at 1809.10 per dollar as traders also worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 President Juan Manuel Santos told a local newspaper this week that a package of measures was on its way. Some analysts have guessed this may include tax relief for exporters.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Caroline Stauffer in Mexico City; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101023e6ak000at\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
