\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 's c.bank not discussing  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 -deputy\b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2010\par 17:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Miner rescue could boost the economy\par \par \uc2 * Peso has overstepped boundary of fundamentals\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not discussion \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment\par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT, Oct 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not currently discussing \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite a view the peso is overvalued, Deputy Governor Manuel Marfan said on Tuesday, while the feel-good factor from last week's mining rescue could boost the economy.\par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=CL> has jumped 14 percent against the dollar since June and was cited as one of the reasons for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the pace of interest rate rises last week.\par \par \uc2 "The (peso) exchange rate has been appreciating and it is at the boundary (of fundamentals) or has even slightly surpassed that," Marfan told reporters on the sidelines of a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conference.\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  he said: "That's something that I should say officially that we have not discussed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far, but the issue is being discussed at the country level."\par \par \uc2 "Usually when you decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  it is because you think you will be successful."\par \par \uc2 He added the risk of a global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war had been overstated, but warned it could not be ruled out and said it could be extremely damaging for Chile.\par \par \uc2 Economic growth might come in slightly above recent forecasts of 5 to 6 percent, but it would not overly impact the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assessment of the economy, Marfan also said.\par \par \uc2 Last week's rescue of 33 miners trapped underground for over two months could give the economy a boost, he said, adding it may also carry risks.\par \par \uc2 "Economy has a lot things that have to do with mood, with perceptions, with expectations and I think when you are successful with something, that's going to give you much more confidence in the rest of the things you do," he said.\par \par \uc2 "The rest of the world is caring about us, and to be true I don't know whether that is good or bad. It's not good to be the pet."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Marc Jones; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 CHILE/MARFAN (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101019e6aj00178\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
