\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's Marfan:Haven't Discussed Peso  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 168 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2010\par 18:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't discussed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, despite the peso's recent rise, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vice governor said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "We have not discussed it at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far, but the issue is being discussed at a country level," Manuel Marfan told reporters on the sidelines of a conference in Frankfurt.\par \par \uc2 He said the Chilean peso has come close to, or slightly surpassed levels, that would be justified in light of the country's economic outlook.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate has been appreciating and is now almost in the boundary, or has slightly surpassed [long-term fundamentals]," Marfan said.\par \par \uc2 The peso last week traded at 29-month highs. It weakened to CLP485.80 to the dollar Tuesday, versus Monday's close of CLP481.00 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Nina Koeppen, Dow Jones Newswires; +49 171 569 4340; nina.koeppen@dowjones.com [ 10-19-10 1208ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020101019e6aj0006x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
