\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends 1.3% Weaker After China Rate Hike, Copper Fall\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2010\par 18:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso weakened sharply against the dollar Tuesday, ending 1.3% weaker, after China caught investors off-guard with an interest rate hike, international copper prices slipped and the Finance Minister reiterated concern on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 The peso, which was recently trading at 29-month highs, weakened to CLP487.00 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP481.00 to the dollar. It traded in a wide range of CLP482.40 to CLP487.50.\par \par \uc2 With China's rate hike stoking fears about a possible global slowdown, the safe-harbor dollar jumped sharply against its major rivals, including the euro.\par \par \uc2 Chile's economy is highly export dependent and a third of its exports are bound for Europe, so the peso takes trading cues from the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also, the peso takes direction from international copper prices as the South American nation produces a third of the world's copper.\par \par \uc2 Copper futures in New York plunged 3% after China's rate hike, as short-term fears about demand from the world's biggest copper consumer overwhelmed a positive longer-term outlook.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, exporters in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been clamoring for market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , arguing that the peso's appreciation is eating into the competitiveness of their products.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, Finance Minister Felipe Larrain said in a seminar that the government was concerned about the peso's strength, especially regarding the impact on agricultural exporters.\par \par \uc2 He said the government was "studying what alternatives it had [to mitigate the peso's strength] and will likely have something to report on that later in the week."\par \par \uc2 Only the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is autonomous, can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. However, the government, through the finance ministry, can take different measures to help moderate the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 "Larrain said the government was going to take some measure, that's not exactly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the market reacted to his comments anyhow," Gloria Soto, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with FXCM Chile said.\par \par \uc2 Also, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vice governor Manuel Marfan, earlier in the day, didn't rule out future market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if justified. Though, he did admit that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't yet discussed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed ahead of an auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign debt scheduled for Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.66%, from 2.67% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 3.07%, from 3.06% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 19-10-10 1720GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dok