\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2  President:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Can't Be Ruled Out\b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2010\par 23:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with additional comments from De Gregorio)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but there would be high costs to pay, bank president Jose De Gregorio said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 As the peso is trading at two-year highs against the dollar, exporters--whose livelihood depends on a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 --are clamoring for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the past 10 years, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times, when it has considered that the peso's exchange rate, in real terms, has deviated from long-term fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 At a gathering of the Fedefruta fruit exporters trade group, De Gregorio called \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "a valid tool," adding that the bank's governing council "evaluates the decision [to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] and undoubtedly, this is something that's been at the forefront of our recent discussions."\par \par \uc2 He noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be very expensive as it requires sterilizing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases so as to not deviate the effects of monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 In his prepared remarks, he also said the peso, in real terms, was slightly below the average it had posted in the previous two decades.\par \par \uc2 Defending the peso's free float adopted in the late 1990s, the central banker said that floating a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbed speculation and massive capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 "We haven't seen any evidence of short-term speculative inflows to arbitrate with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio later presented the same speech to a special session of the lower house of Congress convened to address the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 In his second presentation of the day, he added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could slow down the pace at which it has been withdrawing its monetary stimulus so as to not put further pressure on the peso.\par \par \uc2 "We also consider the effects of exchange rate variations on our inflation outlook and our monetary policy," he said.\par \par \uc2 He noted that a floating exchange rate policy "carried out pragmatically, is the exchange system that's best suited to our reality."\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 10-06-10 1705ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020101006e6a60006q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
