\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECT: \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso May Continue Firming But  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Imminent\b0\par\par\uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2010\par 18:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ("=\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  Peso May Continue Firming But \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Not Imminent," at 5:01 p.m. Friday and repeated at 7:37 a.m. EDT Monday, misstated the strength of the peso in the second paragraph. The correct version follows:)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    By Anthony Esposito \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--With the Chilean peso continuing to rise, and currently at a 28-month high against the dollar, exporters and key political players are increasing pressure for market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, won't likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the peso, in real terms, is still considerably weaker than it was the last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts and traders say.\par \par \uc2 For the year, the peso has gained 5.1% on the dollar, and a much steeper 9.6% since midyear on a rally in global copper prices to two-year highs and broad international dollar weakness.\par \par \uc2 Also fueling the peso's gains are expectations for Chile's economy to continue to quickly recover from last year's recession and February's devastating earthquake and growing spread between local and U.S. interest rates. Chile's benchmark rate is currently at 2.5% and expected to reach 5% next year.\par \par \uc2 As Chile's economy is highly dependent on exports, especially the agricultural and industrial sectors, and the strength of the peso cuts into the competitiveness of those products, exporters have stepped up demands for measures to be taken.\par \par \uc2 Most recently, Chilean agricultural workers threatened general protests if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the peso market, while the conservative UDI political party, which is part of the governing coalition, asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of the negative effect the peso's strength is having on agricultural and industrial sectors.\par \par \uc2 According to a poll released recently, 80% of exporters belonging to the nations' Asexma exporters trade group feel their business is at risk because of the strength of the peso.\par \par \uc2 The poll also highlighted that 85% of exporters questioned said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the peso firms past the CLP480-mark.\par \par \uc2 With the peso closing at CLP481.00 Friday, and soon expected to breach the CLP480 barrier, its climb to CLP470 and beyond looks like it's just a matter of time, traders say.\par \par \uc2 Despite exporters demands for market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders and analysts alike don't see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaling its willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the peso strengthens to CLP460-470. Some analysts even say the range is closer to CLP445-CLP450.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio has said the peso, in real terms, is in line with long-term fundamentals and President Sebastian Pinera said the peso was on a "normal path" despite its relative strength to the dollar. However, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rodrigo Vergara said in prepared remarks that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't rule out capital controls, even though the effectiveness of these measures can be disputed.\par \par \uc2 Over the last decade the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market three times, and the last time it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in April 2008, the peso was trading at 10-year highs against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "At some point if the peso continues to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take a harder stance and verbalize its willingness to act," said Sergio Tricio, head of studies with local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile.\par \par \uc2 The questionable effectiveness of Brazil's and Japan's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, however, provides fodder for those who argue against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the dollar continued its fall against the yen, hovering around a new post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  low of Y83.15 and fell against the Brazilian real to its weakest since Sept. 3, 2008--days before the fall of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  touched off the worst financial crisis in 70 years.\par \par \uc2 "The way markets are reading this is that market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only provide a short term solution, but it won't be too effective over the medium or long term considering the dollar's overall [international] weakness," said Tricio.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 04-10-10 1621GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101004e6a40013x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
