\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Government,  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Meet Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Calls\b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2010\par 23:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Felipe Larrain and Jose de Gregorio, the president of the nation's autonomous \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , held a "regular coordination meeting" Monday, Larrain said. The meeting came amid rising demands for the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's President Sebastian Pinera called on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to better coordinate its monetary and exchange rate policies with the government's fiscal and macroeconomic policies in order to have a competitive exchange rate that helps exporters, and the agricultural sector in particular.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an independent body and has complete autonomy over its decisions.\par \par \uc2 "The government, through the Finance Ministry, has worried about implementing solid, responsible and balanced macroeconomic and fiscal spending policies, so as to not negatively pressure key economic variables such as the exchange rate, interest rates and inflation," Larrain said.\par \par \uc2 As Chile's economy is highly dependent on exports and the strength of the peso hurts the competitiveness of those products, exporters are demanding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The peso was trading at a 28-month high prior to Pinera's call and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rodrigo Vergara's recent assertion that "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is a tool that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't rule out, although it is only used in exceptional circumstances."\par \par \uc2 After Pinera's and Vergara's comments, the peso weakened 1.1% Monday, ending at CLP486.40 to the dollar, compared to Friday's close of CLP481.00.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 04-10-10 2158GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101004e6a40018l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
