\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2 : Not Now Says \uc2 JP Morgan\b0\par\par\uc2 1,267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2010\par 14:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1204 GMT [Dow Jones] Whereas other central banks are moving to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in their local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, the Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will remain hands-off for the time being, \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. "The hurdle for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is a moving target and not a line in the sand...the peso is far from the type of misalignment that justified \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past," the investment bank added. It sees the Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moving towards market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the peso continues to firm to CLP445 to CLP450, compared to many other analysts' estimates of a CLP460-470 range. Exporters have been clamouring for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the stronger peso hurts the competitiveness of their products. The peso ended unchanged Wednesday, just shy of a 27-month high, at 485.50 to the dollar. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1200 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro Overnight Index Average fixed lower Wednesday at 0.408% versus Tuesday's 0.425%. Thursday, the interbank overnight rate is trading higher between 0.40% and 0.70%. A money dealer says with regard to the wide range that "the market is very chaotic at the moment," pointing to the end of a one-year tender. Earlier Thursday, 3-month Euribor fixed at 0.892% vs 0.886% Wednesday. (herbert.rude@dowjones.com) Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 1144 GMT [Dow Jones] Rising food prices in Brazil shouldn't affect consumer price inflation unless it turns into "significantly high and protracted food inflation," says RBS Securities. The inflation of manufactured goods at the wholesale level is likely to remain tame, anchored by low inflation abroad and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, RBS says. "Still, for the time being, given that food inflation is on a rise and is unlikely to moderate anytime soon, we should be prepared for adverse inflation surprises in the upcoming weeks," RBS says. (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1130 GMT [Dow Jones] Calif gov race very close with Democrat Jerry Brown (37%) and Republican Meg Whitman (38%) in a virtual tie among likely voters, with 18% undecided, a survey from Public Policy Institute of Calif. says. In U.S. Senate race, incumbent Barbara Boxer leads Republican Carly Fiorina 42%-35%, with 17% undecided. Despite declaration that national recession is over, 89% of residents say Calif is in recession, and 62% say jobs and economy are most important issue. Approval ratings of state and federal elected officials at or near record lows, PPIC said, and only 45% are satisfied with choice of candidates in governor's race. (stan.rosenberg@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1056 GMT [Dow Jones] The U.S. data slate is beginning to get exciting, notes \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . The week's most important data release, the ISM index is just a day away but beforehand comes today's Chicago PMI index at 1345 GMT, which acts as a leading indicator for the former, albeit a poor indicator. Other data of note Thursday are the 2Q GDP revision and initial jobless claims at 1230 GMT. \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says the same applies to all three data releases: only notable positive surprises will prevent the Fed from QE2. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1039 GMT [Dow Jones] The prospect of weak euro zone peripheral PMIs on Friday and an offered USD/JPY suggests significant risk of a downside correction in EUR/JPY says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . Now at 113.85 the bank says a break below the 112.85 support area could be the trigger for such a move. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1021 GMT [Dow Jones] Euribor futures fall after the ECB's 6-day tender received lower demand than expected Thursday at EUR29.3 billion versus around EUR70 billion forecast by the market. This leaves excess liquidity much lower at between EUR15-40 billion, sending eonia swaps higher and euribor futures lower. The December '10 euribor falls 4 bps to 98.95, March '11 falls 5 bps to 98.84, June '11 falls 4 bps to 98.75 and September '11 falls 4 bps to 98.68. One-month eonia is up 2.5 bps at 0.56%, three-month eonia is up 2.5 bps at 0.62%, six-months is up 4 bps at 0.69% and 12-month eonia is 5 bps higher at 0.81%. (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1020 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR falls to 39-month low as foreign funds continue to flow into local debt, stock markets, dealers say. Pair last at 8,920 vs 8,910 earlier, 8,935 late yesterday. "The pair is heavily biased down, and it could have hit 8,900 if the Bank Indonesia didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," dealer says. Adds, BI may have bought around $200 million to stem IDR's rise. 8,900-8,930 range tipped for Friday. "Near-term, KRW, PHP, IDR and THB may continue to perform well on capital inflows and external balances," says Standard Chartered.(andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1020 GMT [Dow Jones] December bunds are down 0.05 at 131.76 and Nick Holt, a trader at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  cautions that momentum is showing signs of running out of steam. "If we cannot break back into the up-channel and close above 132.14, then a retrace will be on the horizon," he says. Support is at 131.53, 131.46, and 131.32. Resistance is at 132.00, 132.20, and 132.50. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1018 GMT [Dow Jones] The Irish government has repeated its reassurances to Anglo Irish senior bondholders Thursday, but \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  "can not help thinking that Anglo's senior debt should be subjected to a haircut too." Argues that the benefits to the sovereign ("by putting a stop to the money drain") would indirectly support \uc2 Bank of Ireland\uc2  and Allied Irish spreads, outweighing concerns that they too might be subject to a haircut at some stage. CDS written on Anglo Irish's senior debt were 25 bps tighter Thursday at 860 bps, while sub CDS were at 51 points upfront, 7 points higher, according to Markit. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1004 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex +0.8% at 20,107.60 as investors cover short positions ahead of close of derivate expiry for September. "Volumes have picked up sharply in banks and metal shares. These are the real contributors to the benchmark index's rise," says local dealer; adds, "funds are continuing to look for good investments at lower levels and this is one main reason for the short covering." Among gainers, HDFC (500010.BY) +3.3% at INR729.30, ITC (500875.BY) +2.7% at INR178.40, \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2  (500112.BY) +2.0% at INR3,256, \uc2 Sterlite Industries\uc2  +3.2% at INR166.60. Sensex tipped in 19,800-20,200 range Friday. (raghavendra.upadhyaya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1002 GMT [Dow Jones] South Africa's PPI reading for August was a touch higher than consensus expectations, but with little pass-through into CPI this isn't likely to trigger meaningful reaction, says Standard Chartered's Razia Khan. He adds: "It is a small point in favor of rates staying on hold, but PPI was never going to be the make or break factor." Annual PPI was up 7.8% after a rise of 7.7% in July. (robb.stewart@dowjones.com) [ 09-30-10 0804ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100930e69u0007j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
