\par\par \b \uc2 Chile exporters urge cenbank to curb strong peso\b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2010\par 02:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Exporters says stronger peso eats away profits\par \par \uc2 * Firms see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 480 pesos/dlr - poll\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank has signaled no immediate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Sept 28 (Reuters) - Exporters in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a major producer of fruit, wine and wood pulp, on Tuesday urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and curb a rapidly appreciating peso that has hurt profits.\par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=CL> <CLP=> is trading at over 2-year highs of 480.50 per dollar as the economy of the world's top copper producer picks up steam amid a sluggish global recovery.\par \par \uc2 A stronger peso has weighed on the revenues of local exporters that are paid in dollars for their sales abroad.\par \par \uc2 The Manufacturing and Services Exporters Association, or Asexma, said exporters are quickly losing ground against competitors abroad due to a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A poll released by the trade group showed that more than 85 percent of the firms surveyed believe the bank should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the peso passes 480 per dollar. The survey included executives at 112 companies within the trade group during August and September.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 TAKE-A-LOOK on Chile's economic recovery [ID:nN30113748]\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has so far brushed aside talks of an immediate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it reiterated late last week that the peso is in line with long-term fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Still, bank President Jose de Gregorio has said future rate hikes would be faster without a strong peso, hinting of smaller rate increases that could take away some of the peso momentum.\par \par \uc2 A growing differential between rates in Chile and those in the United States and Europe has lured droves of investors looking for a quick profit, exponentially increasing dollar inflows and strengthening the peso.\par \par \uc2 Bank board member Rodrigo Vergara said in a speech published on Monday that emerging countries cannot rule out capital controls to ease \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but acknowledge its "effectiveness is even more disputed" than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The government of President Sebastian Pinera has said it plans to slow public spending, which could in turn help stem the sharp appreciation of the peso. (Reporting by Alonso Soto; Editing by Richard Chang)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/EXPORTERS|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100929e69t00010\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
