\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: RBC Sees Reduced Risk Of  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,126 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2010\par 17:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1531 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's push to become a regional financial hub, as it integrates stock exchange with bourses in Peru and Colombia, and its potential move to make the peso a deliverable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  --so it can be bought and sold everywhere-- decreases the likelihood the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a report. Exporters in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been clamouring for market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the peso has risen to 27-month highs against the dollar, hurting the competitiveness of their products. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1523 GMT [Dow Jones] Similar to other rate futures markets, there's been little change so far this session in fed-funds futures. Expectations for next round of quantitative easing means market is almost certain there won't be tightening of funds rate next autumn. Nov '11 contract prices in 24% chance for FOMC to raise funds rate to 0.5% at next Nov's meeting, near the 22% odds priced in at Tues' settlement. Same contract priced in 32% chance Monday. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1517 GMT [Dow Jones] Long-dated Treasurys down again in volatile trade as market digests comments from Fed officials and in preparation for $29B 7-yr sale at 1 p.m. ET. Last night, Fed's Lockhart said it was "not a foreone conclusion" that aid from the Fed to stimulate the economy was necessary, and today, Fed's Kocherlakota said more asset purchases would have limited impact and a rate hike would be more likely before asset purchases unwound. Neither are voters this year. 10-yr is 2/32 lower to yield 2.478%; 7-yr is 2/32 lower to yield 1.852%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1521 GMT [Dow Jones] The statement by Poland's Monetary Policy Council following its decision to keep it's key rates at 3.50% Wednesday, as expected, is more hawkish than prior ones, \uc2 Bank Millennium\uc2  says. That's because the MPC has stressed the role of "inflationary expectations," which means "the MPC sees the need to act before the inflation rise," the bank says. The MPC also seems to be very divided, with parts of its ten members favoring a 50-basis-point hike and parts seeing no need for such action. "One can't rule out [the possibility that] tightening will be delayed," Millennium says. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1512 GMT [Dow Jones] Muni market under a tad bit of pressure, as it digests a number of offerings that are pricing Wed, says \uc2 Miller Tabak\uc2  CEO Michael Pietronico. "There's no one deal" that's getting the market's attention because "there's too many of them. To me, it's just watching all of them and seeing how they do," Pietronico said. Debt sales in market range from around $20M to around $500M or more, he added. Looking ahead, NJ slated to sell around $1B in GOs Thurs. Retail order period starts today on $592M tax-exempt piece offered in two series; 2021 maturity offers 5% coupon and 2.92% yield. (kelly.nolan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1509 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish treasury bonds are stronger following the Monetary Policy Council's decision to keep rates at 3.50%, as expected. T-bonds recover after some volatility. A delay in the decision's announcement triggered speculation of a rate hike. Average yield on 2-year bonds is at 4.69% from 4.73% late Tuesday, 5-year at 5.05% from 5.09%, 10-year at 5.47% versus 5.50% late Tuesday. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1508 GMT [Dow Jones] Emerging market bonds strengthen after a few days of weakness. Turkey--after the finance minister said fiscal performance may top government targets--and Venezuela--after the opposition gained power in elections--are leading the drive up. The risk premium on \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's Emerging Markets Bond Index Global is 10 bps tighter to 306 bps over Tsys. The index is up 0.35%. Brazil's benchmark bond, the Global 2040, is up 1/16 to 138 9/16 bid, according to Reuters. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1507 GMT [Dow Jones] A construction boom that has been leading the strong pace of economic growth in Peru is set to continue, expanding by an expected 15.6% this year, a leading business group said. The Lima Chamber of Commerce, which forecasts an overall expansion in Peru's gross domestic product of this year of 7.9%, pointed out that mortgage loans have been growing at a double-digit pace this year. (robert.kozak@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1508 GMT [Dow Jones] The decision of Poland's Monetary Policy Council to keep rates at 3.50% is not surprising, Bank Pekao says. "Our basic scenario sees a possibility of a rate hike next month, which is in line with the market consensus," the bank says. "However, the decision will depend on new domestic and global macroeconomic data." (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1458 GMT [Dow Jones] Aviation Capital Group is preparing to sell $300M 10-year bonds late Wednesday or Thursday via joint bookrunners \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  and \uc2 J.P.Morgan Chase\uc2 , according to a person familiar with the sale. The bonds are expected to be rated BBB- by S&P and Fitch and proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes. (katy.burne@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1458 GMT [Dow Jones] Nordea recommends hedging HUF revenues for the short term "using forwards" amid uncertainties around what the government's rhetoric will be after local elections coming on Sunday. HUF could face a new round of weakness in the short run says Nordea, if the bank's negative global macroeconomic outlook for the autumn is correct. A slight change of rhetoric from the government would be enough to bring relief to Hungary's markets, it notes. EUR/HUF at 276.90. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1454 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys have handed investors a return of 0.2% this month through Tuesday, according to data from \uc2 Barclays\uc2 . The rally in recent sessions amid QE2 buzz has helped the market recover from losses earlier in September. Yet the return pales in comparison with junk bonds which handed investors a return of 2.75% over the same period. US stocks are big winners with the benchmark S&P gaining 9.37%. Even TIPS are doing better with a 1.6% return. The loser this month is MBS which was down 0.29% over the same period. Munis broke even so far. (min.zeng@dowjones.com) [ 09-29-10 1131ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100929e69t000av\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
