\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks Close Lower On Profit Taking, US Market Slump\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 752 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2010\par 22:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index closed lower Wednesday as investors booked profits and the local market tracked slumping U.S. stocks.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa ended 0.5% lower at 4782.83, while market volume rose to 93.3 billion Chilean pesos ($192.1 million) compared with CLP88.3 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 With the Ipsa again breaking the 4800-point barrier the prior session and nearing its all-time high, institutional investors took advantage of the high prices to book profits.\par \par \uc2 "There's a shuffling of investment portfolios, institutional investors are selling shares and taking profits," said Rodrigo Arriagada, trader with local brokerage Molina y Swett.\par \par \uc2 Also, as several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average. The DJIA ended 0.2% lower at 10835.28.\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, specialty chemical and fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM, SQM-B.SN) more liquid B-series shares (SQM-B.SN) fell 3.2% to CLP23,447.00 after \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  downgraded the stock from neutral to underperform.\par \par \uc2 "SQM slipped on the downgrade today, but over the long term the company's prospects still look good as does demand for its products," said Arriagada.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, Chilean bank \uc2 CorpBanca\uc2  (BCA, CORPBANCA.SN) dropped 4.4% to CLP7.30 after saying it's negotiating the sale of "no more than 10%" of its shares to Brazilian government-owned \uc2 Banco do Brasil SA\uc2  (BBAS3.BR). Prior to Wednesday's drop, \uc2 CorpBanca\uc2 , which is owned by the local Saieh family, had risen 10.3% over the last week on speculation \uc2 Banco do Brasil\uc2  could acquire part or all of its shares.\par \par \uc2 Holding company \uc2 Hipermarc\uc2  (HIPERMARC.SN), which is also owned by the Saieh family and holds the Unimarc supermarket chain, surged 59.3% to CLP27.08. Participants hoped the Corpbanca stake sale would give \uc2 Hipermarc\uc2 's owners cash in hand for new investments. \uc2 Hipermarc\uc2  isn't on the Ipsa, but is listed on the general stock index.\par \par \uc2 Among other decliners, retailer La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN) declined 0.8% to CLP3,615.00, while the nation's largest bank \uc2 Banco Santander Chile\uc2  (SAN, BSANTANDE.SN) lost 1.0% to CLP45.40 as investors took profits in two of the sectors which have consistently led the Ipsa's record run this year.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, for a second straight session, the peso ended flat against the dollar--near a 27-month high--as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to break a key resistance level.\par \par \uc2 The peso came back off its earlier highs to end unchanged at CLP485.50 to the dollar. It traded in a tight range of CLP484.60 to CLP486.00.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose early in the session as international copper prices hit a 25-month high. Because Chile produces over one-third of global copper, the peso often takes cues from the metal's international prices.\par \par \uc2 After the peso failed to break through key resistance at CLP483-CLP484, however, it retreated from its earlier gains.\par \par \uc2 As the strength of the peso cuts into the competitiveness of Chilean exports and the local economy is highly dependent on its exports, exporters' demands for market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have become louder.\par \par \uc2 Traders think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the peso strengthens past CLP470.\par \par \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 , however, thinks the likelihood the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been reduced as \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushes to become a regional financial hub-- with the Santiago Stock Exchange integrating with bourses in Peru and Colombia--and as the nation moves toward making the peso a deliverable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so it can be bought and sold everywhere.\par \par \uc2 "Only the Mexican peso can be traded overnight, but it seems Chile is moving in that direction, too, as it looks to become a financial hub," said Eduardo Suarez of \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 ' emerging-markets research team.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher following a scheduled auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued sovereign debt.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.73%, from 2.66% Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 3.03%, from 2.95% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 29-09-10 2047GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100929e69t001fs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
