\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-Chile rate hikes faster without strong peso-cenbank\b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2010\par 17:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * De Gregorio hints at slower rate hikes- analysts\par \par \uc2 * Peso trades at over two-year highs to the dollar\par \par \uc2 * Analysts differ on peso levels for cenbank to step in\par \par \uc2 By Antonio de la Jara and Brad Haynes\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Sept 24 (Reuters) Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hike its benchmark interest rate faster if it were not for the strengthening of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to a speech by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio, who spoke at a banking conference held by the \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago\uc2 , said the peso <CLP=CL> had appreciated "significantly" in recent weeks due to the increase of capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 His comments could signal a slowdown in future rate hikes after the bank started an aggressive upcycle in June to preempt inflationary pressures amid a rapid economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 "Although in our latest Monetary Policy Report we said that the bank will keep withdrawing the significant monetary stimulus, without the strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the withdrawal would certainly be faster," according to the text of the speech delivered on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso is trading at over two-year highs against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the economy of the world's top copper producer picks up and the greenback has weakened across the board.\par \par \uc2 The peso's sharp appreciation has prompted analysts and traders to talk of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ TAKE-A-LOOK \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy recovery [ID:nN30113748] ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio said in his speech that exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot be ruled out when there is a misalignment of the exchange rate plus huge capital inflows that "may be the prelude of problems, in the extreme a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  or financial meltdown."\par \par \uc2 He added that capital inflows may be a source of bubbles in the domestic asset prices in the emerging countries, many of which are growing faster than developed nations amid a slow global recovery.\par \par \uc2 Juan Pablo Castro, an economist with Santander GBM in Santiago, said it was too soon to say if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would slow its rate hikes from the 50 basis-point pace of the past four months but De Gregorio has raised the possibility.\par \par \uc2 "Clearly if this appreciation of the peso continues and the consumer price index for September comes in below expectations, there we could see a 25 basis-point hike," Castro said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Enrique Marshall said in a presentation released earlier on Friday that the peso <CLP=CL> <CLP=> when compared to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in real terms is in line with long-term fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended 0.41 percent higher on Friday at 486.50/487.00 per dollar, extending a two-day rally.\par \par \uc2 Interest rate futures show the market expects Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise its benchmark rate by 50 basis points for a fifth straight month in October to 3.0 percent, attracting more inflows of foreign capital and strengthening the peso.\par \par \uc2 President Sebastian Pinera said on Wednesday the exchange rate between the peso and the dollar was at normal levels and there was no immediate need for government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nN22256063]\par \par \uc2 The wider weakness of the dollar is driving much of the peso's rally as the dollar index <.DXY>, which tracks the performance of the greenback against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has dropped nearly 8 percent in the last eight months.\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/CENBANK (WRAPUP 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100924e69o001fb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
