\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Chile's Pinera: Doing 'Everything Possible' For Trapped Miners\b0\par\par\uc2 721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2010\par 19:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2010 13:24 EDT *DJ  Chile's Pinera: Committed To Growth Recovery; 2010 GDP Seen At 6%\par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2010 13:41 EDT *DJ  Chile's Pinera: Miners May Be Rescued Earlier Than Expected, November\par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2010 13:50 EDT *DJ  Chile's Pinera: Would Like US To Move Faster On FTAs In Latin America\par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2010 13:50 EDT *DJ  Chile's Pinera: Don't Expect Chile Will Borrow Much In Global Bond Markets\par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2010 13:51 EDT *DJ  Chile's Pinera: Will Issue Global Bonds Before End Of Government's Term\par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2010 13:52 EDT *DJ  Chile's Pinera: Will Be Active In Capital Markets To Add Value To Raw Material Exports\par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2010 13:53 EDT *DJ  Chile Pinera: Exchange Rate Is Normal; No Major Changes In Future\par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2010 13:53 EDT *DJ  Chile Pinera: Don't Want To Jeopardize Exports With Rising \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2010 13:54 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  Pinera: \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Has Tools To \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , But Peso On 'Normal Path'\par \par \uc2 22 Sep 2010 14:38 EDT DJ  Chile's Pinera: Peso On 'Normal Path'; Sees 6% 2010 GDP Growth\par \par \uc2 By Riva Froymovich\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Chile's strengthening peso remains on a "normal path," although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the tools to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets if necessary, said Chilean President Sebastian Pinera on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The peso has been fast appreciating against the U.S. dollar as U.S. interest rates remain low, leading investors to chase higher yields in emerging markets. Chile's economy is also growing faster, providing an alternative to the stagnant developed world.\par \par \uc2 "If you grow faster than the rest of the world your \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to appreciate," said Pinera, particularly given the price of copper, the country's top export, is at elevated levels.\par \par \uc2 He was speaking at an Americas Society and Council of the Americas event in New York.\par \par \uc2 Pinera said strong fiscal policy will protect the economy from the effects of a rising peso, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the tools to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary.\par \par \uc2 The peso was recently near a 35-week high at CLP493.70 to the dollar, versus Tuesday's close at CLP497.20, according to Valor Futuro newswire.\par \par \uc2 Pinera also repeated forecasts for Chile's gross domestic product to grow 6% this year, and said the country may even surprise economists to the upside. He said inflation isn't a concern, and the country's growth rates are sustainable.\par \par \uc2 Due to the country's high savings, Pinera doesn't expect the government to issue much more in global bonds after selling debt to international markets for the first time in six years this past July.\par \par \uc2 Chile issued the notes to provide guidance for its private sector, he said.\par \par \uc2 Pinera said, however, that Chile could again issue debt before the end of his government's term. He added that the country will be active in capital markets to "add value" to its massive raw material exports.\par \par \uc2 Chile is among the top global copper exports.\par \par \uc2 Those resources have attracted huge investment and trade with China, which receives about 25% of Chile's exports, said Pinera.\par \par \uc2 He said Chile's growth strategy relies on open and competitive trade. Pinera added that he would like to see the U.S. move faster on furthering those principles through free-trade agreements with other Latin American nations, such as Colombia and Panama.\par \par \uc2 Pinera repeated the goals of his administration for the next four years and for the next decade. He aims to defeat poverty, double investment in education, reform the health-care system, and create 1 million jobs.\par \par \uc2 "We are very confident we can achieve our goals," he said.\par \par \uc2 Separately, Pinera said 33 workers trapped in a mine since August may be rescued earlier than expected, in the beginning of November.\par \par \uc2 Pinera took office in March, after a massive magnitude 8.8 earthquake and ensuing tsunami that killed hundreds, left tens of thousands homeless and caused damages upwards of $30 billion, roughly 18% of GDP.\par \par \uc2 -By Riva Froymovich, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2217; riva.froymovich@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 22, 2010 14:38 ET (18:38 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100922e69m00402\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
