\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Stronger On US Econ Data,  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Comments\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 20:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended slightly stronger against the dollar Thursday on encouraging U.S. jobs and trade deficit data as well as the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments that it isn't likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 After paring back some of its earlier gains, the peso ended stronger at CLP496.00 to the dollar, compared to Wednesday's close of CLP496.50. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP493.40 and CLP496.50.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely tied to the pace of global growth gained after better-than-expected U.S. data painted a brighter picture of the economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 As Europe is one of Chile's main trade partners, the peso often moves in the same direction as the euro does against the dollar. The euro posted a small gain against the greenback.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tempered speculation about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. With exporters clamouring that the peso's relative strength versus the dollar is hurting the competitiveness of their products, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio said Wednesday that Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in line with its fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Although analysts see the peso moving toward CLP492 in the short term, the peso again bounced back, giving up most of its gains, after hitting a key level of resistance located around CLP493-CLP494.\par \par \uc2 "If the peso doesn't manage to break resistance we'll probably see the peso stuck trading in a short range of CLP494 to CLP498," said Gloria Soto, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with FXCM Chile.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher after banks placed stop-loss orders.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended higher at 2.45%, from 2.37% Wednesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs ended higher at 2.81% from 2.72% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 09-09-10 1810GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100909e699001g5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
