\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Conditions Favor Exploration Gold Stocks - TD\b0\par\par\uc2 1,264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 16:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 10:50 (Dow Jones) September's usually seasonally strong for gold and gold stocks, and with the sector enjoying a spat of recent deal making, TD figures exploration gold companies and those developing mines are best situated to benefit from current conditions. These companies are typically more levered to higher gold prices and often takeover targets for larger players seeking growth, firm says. TD is particularly bullish on Detour Gold (DGC.T), which should complete project permitting and financing within the next year, and \uc2 Extorre Gold Mines\uc2  (XG.T), which has enjoyed drilling success at its gold-silver project in Argentina, TD says. In Toronto, DGC.T recently down 3% at C$29.14; XG.T down 1% at C$5.01. (ben.dummett@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:34 (Dow Jones) Transat's (TRZ.B.T) 3Q results today illustrate that "its business model remains viable," making it "a compelling investment," \uc2 Laurentian Bank\uc2  says. Long-term prospects remain favorable. Sees demand for leisure travel rebounding in line with an economic recovery, while scheduled carriers could remove some capacity from Caribbean and Mexico routes when demand for business travel recovers on domestic and cross-border routes. In Toronto, shares recently up 4% to C$14.30. (caroline.vanhasselt@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:29 (Dow Jones) Macquarie says port traffic jumped in July in both the US and Asia, a sign that freight trends could be pointing to a firmer economic environment. Container shipping volumes in China and the US rose about 20%, but firm is hesitant to draw too much from the data. Points out that last year's comps might provide favorable skew, but says "solid" ocean and North American rail volumes likely in 3Q. Macquarie keeps outperform rating on UPS, CSX, \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  (NSC), Union Pacific (UNP), \uc2 CH Robinson\uc2  (CHRW) and Expeditors Intl (EXPD). (christopher.dieterich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:20 (Dow Jones) A chagrined-sounding top \uc2 Con-way\uc2  (CNW) executive reiterates the trucker is committed to raising prices in the less-than-truckload sector, after admittedly taking a leading role in the race downward last year. "We were at the forefront of some of that pricing aggression," CFO \uc2 Stephen Bruffett\uc2  tells Dahlman Rose conference. CNW has since embarked on a "more sustainable, and perhaps rational, pricing program," he says. The head of CNW's LTL division stepped down last month to pursue "other interests." LTL carriers consolidate loads from multiple customers onto single trucks. CNW up 1.3% at $28.84. (bob.sechler@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:15 (Dow Jones) Citi cuts forecast for US natural gas prices, while raising price outlook for eastern coal. Lowers gas forecast to $4.50/MMBtu from $4.75 for this year; $4.25 from $5.75 next year, amid strong production from onshore shale formations. As for coal, Citi raises 2H forecast for Central Appalachia to $65/ton from $60 as costs increase on tighter safety, environmental regulations. Firm holds forecast of $65/ton next year, while upping price outlook for Powder River Basin coal for next year, 2012. (mark.peters@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:09 (Dow Jones) S&P 500 has rallied to a one-month high, but bulls shouldn't consider that a breakout just yet. Looming just above is the 200-day moving average at around 1115. The S&P 500 closed above the 200-day the first seven sessions in August, but couldn't close more than 11 points above it before tumbling 2.8% on the eighth day. And while the DJIA had no trouble getting above the 200-day in early August, it was capped right at the line the previous three sessions, and is now holding just above it. S&P 500 up 9 at 1108; DJIA up 65 at 10452 vs 200-day at 10450. (tomi.kilgore@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:02 (Dow Jones) Appraisers who value items for tax purposes are noting with interest an upcoming closed-door meeting later this month of an IRS panel on art. The group will look at fair-market appraisals of works of art claimed on federal income, estate or gift tax returns. Judith Martin, president of the International Society of Appraisers, says IRS art experts in general are working more closely with her group since the Pension Protection Act of 2006 raised the bar for valuing charitable donations. (arden.dale@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:55 (Dow Jones) Fortis (FTS.T) is on the verge of a major breakout, says Montreal-based Phases & Cycles. Firm says the gas & electric utility's recent rise to C$30.81 signals higher targets, and a rise above C$31 would "confirm the breakout." Initial targets are C$34 and C$39, with "higher targets visible," firm says. Recently in Toronto, Fortis at C$30.54. (andy.georgiades@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:51 (Dow Jones) Electronic exchange operator BATS Global Markets looking at a range of new asset classes and geographies, but still sees room for growing its core stock-trading franchises in US and Europe, according to Ticonderoga. Management thinks BATS could grab 18% of US cash equities market long term, vs current 10.2%, while its slice of the European pie could treble in size to 15% as London-based unit seen achieving profitability next year. Meanwhile, the company's weighing push into \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and futures, as well as potential stock platforms in Canada and Brazil. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:46 (Dow Jones) \uc2 AT&T\uc2  (T) put more than $275M to work upgrading its wireless network in the New York area during 1H, nearly eclipsing the $290M spent all of last year. T says the result is faster and better wireless in an area hampered by criticism over dropped calls and shoddy reception, partly due to a network overloaded with data-hungry Apple (AAPL) iPhones. T up 1% at $27.65. (paul.ziobro@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:41 (Dow Jones) National Bank Financial suggests four "technical" reasons to take profits in Biovail (BVF), which is up 16% this month alone on higher-than-expected synergies from its merger with Valeant (VRX). Firm says the "flag breakout" at $19 fulfilled its upside objective of $24-$25; yesterday's reversal saw the stock close near its intraday lows after making "new rally highs"; at prices 25% above its 50-day average and 58% above its 200-day average, the stock is "extended"; and the stock turned back after approaching "chart resistance" around $27, indicating an unfavorable risk/reward. BVF up a fraction at $26.62. (andy.georgiades@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:36 (Dow Jones) Chile's peso strengthens against the greenback after the president of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tempered speculation yesterday of imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Faced with clamoring exporters who say peso's relative strength vs USD is hurting the competitiveness of their products, Jose De Gregorio responded that Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in line with its fundamentals. "His comments made it very clear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not looking to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is comfortable with where the peso is currently trading," said Rodrigo Sarria, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local investment bank Celfin Capital. Peso recently at CLP494.90 vs CLP496.50 at yesterday's close. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Equities Market Talk Editors, \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Paul Vigna, 212 416-2184,paul.vigna@dowjones.com \par Visit the Market Talk website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-09-10 1050ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020100909e699000a4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
