\par\par \b \uc2 SNAP ANALYSIS- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso to firm but no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen\b0\par\par\uc2 By Maria Jose Latorre and Alonso Soto   \par \uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2010\par 22:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Sept 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso <CLP=CL> <CLP=> will likely continue to rise in the short-term after hitting new 7-month highs on Wednesday, but gains are seen limited and are not expected to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 For a TAKE-A-LOOK on \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  economy, peso [ID:nN30113748] ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 VOLATILITY AHEAD\par \par \uc2 Stronger global stocks, high copper prices and rising domestic rates will likely boost the peso in the short term, but fears of a double-dip global recession that pushes investors to take refuge in the dollar could keep a lid on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.\par \par \uc2 Uncertainty over copper demand in top consumer China also signals more volatility ahead for prices of copper, by far the main export of world No.1 producer Chile.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say positive local economic data and expected further interest rate hikes have already been factored in by the market as the country steadily recovers from the global downturn and a massive Feb. 27 earthquake.\par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts point to wider dollar strength, global bourses and copper demand as the key drivers for the peso in the coming months.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  UNLIKELY\par \par \uc2 Analysts see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the peso's rise if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises to a range of 480 to 465 per dollar, but expect further gains to fall short of that.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio has not ruled out an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but has said the peso is in line with long-term fundamentals in real terms -- which markets took as a signal there would be no imminent bank action.\par \par \uc2 The peso has appreciated 2.7 percent against the dollar so far this year, with most of the gains posted since July. Last year, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated 26.4 percent after depreciating 22.4 percent in 2008.\par \par \uc2 ABOVE 500/DLR BY YR-END\par \par \uc2 Traders are betting the peso will likely trade 0.18 percent weaker in three months time, compared to the current level, according to non-deliverable forwards or NDFs <CLPNDF=>, a form of derivative.\par \par \uc2 Fears of a slowing global recovery are seen ultimately exerting downward pressure on the peso later this year.\par \par \uc2 The local market sees the peso trading at 507.50 per dollar by year-end and at 500 in three months time, according to the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll of traders and financial players. (Editing by Simon Gardner and Todd Eastham)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/ (SNAP ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100904e691000ca\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
