\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  finance minister warns on peso  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 833 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2010\par 13:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Peso weakens after finance minister's comments\par \par \uc2 * Market bets on continued peso gains\par \par \uc2 * Traders say verbal warnings likely not enough (Updates with peso close, NDF data)\par \par \uc2 By Antonio de la Jara and Simon Gardner\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Aug 19 (Reuters) - Chilean Finance Minister Felipe Larrain on Thursday warned investors that authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem a sharp appreciation of the local peso <CLP=CL> and is coordinating closely with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The peso recently surged to seven-month highs, boosted by strong prices for copper, Chile's top export, and as an interest-rate cycle in tightening mode lures investment. It eased 1 percent on Thursday. For more see, [ID:nN18182427] [ID:nN12145806]\par \par \uc2 Larrain said the government had sought to avoid pressuring the peso in recent months by structuring a plan to finance reconstruction after a massive February earthquake to minimize impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said there were factors the government could not control.\par \par \uc2 He conceded there was limited scope for government action.\par \par \uc2 "The government is doing what it can on its part to avoid additional appreciation," Larrain told state television, referring to the fact the government has not repatriated hundreds of millions of dollars raised by an international bond issue.\par \par \uc2 "If the price of copper rises strongly, if the U.S. economy is growing weakly and there are no expectations of a rise in (U.S.) rates, it is very difficult to battle against that," he said. <------------------------------------------------------ For Chile peso scenarios, see [ID:nN19249922] For a Chile peso graphic, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/wex55n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/wex55n}}}\uc2  For a Latam \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  graphic, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/ged55n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/ged55n}}}\uc2  ------------------------------------------------------->\par \par \uc2 Benchmark interest rates in the United States remain near zero percent and are not seen rising anytime soon. By contrast, Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised its benchmark rate three times since June to 2.0 percent currently, and the market is betting on another rise of 50 basis points next month.\par \par \uc2 A continuing surge in the peso would make Chile's exports less competitive, which could put the brakes on the economy's recovery from the February earthquake and from the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Larrain cited examples of past \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "In the past, there have been exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cases which were considered extreme," he said. "Those \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are never announced beforehand, only after they happen."\par \par \uc2 However, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its last major \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2008 after the peso appreciated sharply amid a commodity boom, it gave the market a clear calendar outlining plans to buy $8 billion dollars via auction.\par \par \uc2 The peso eased after Larrain spoke, deepening losses on the back of poor U.S. jobs data.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed 1.1 percent weaker at 507.30/507.80 per dollar compared with Wednesday's close. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is up around 8 percent since the end of June. [ID:nN19267404]\par \par \uc2 Traders are betting the peso will appreciate by a miniscule 0.01 percent over the next month, according to the non-deliverable forwards market <CLPNDF=>, a form of derivatives trading popular outside Chile due to the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls.\par \par \uc2 But the peso is expected to then erase those gains and gradually weaken against the U.S. dollar in the months ahead. The NDF market indicates the peso will depreciate 0.06 percent in two months' time and trade 0.18 percent weaker in three months' time, compared with the current level.\par \par \uc2 Larrain had voiced similar concerns about the strong peso on Wednesday, which followed on the heels of comments by President Sebastian Pinera about the exchange rate last week.\par \par \uc2 Market players suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the peso's rally continues much further.\par \par \uc2 "Below 500 pesos per dollar, the authorities will get nervous and could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but so far these are just warning shots," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer.\par \par \uc2 "The market tends to react to this sort of comment, but if it does not see concrete action, things resume their course, and so far, we have just seen words," he added.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts believe the bank would only move if the peso firmed beyond 480 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect South American policy makers to step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but caution that doing so risks stoking inflation and say it could ultimately put the brakes on a regional interest rate up-cycle. [ID:N17270580]\par \par \uc2 Peru has aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year to counter sharp gains by its sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <PEN=PE>, which is around two-year highs, while Colombia is looking at measures to give businesses relief from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength. [ID:nN18206932]\par \par \uc2 And some analysts believe Brazil could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to counter strength in its real <BRBY> \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the psychologically important 1.75 per dollar level is broken for a sustained period. [ID:nN19252564] (Additional reporting by Froilan Romero and Samantha Pearson in Sao Paulo; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100819e68j000s7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
