\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile, Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  break key levels\b0\par\par\uc2 671 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2010\par 17:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Bond flows support region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real firms 0.3 pct, Mexican peso flat\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso pares gains after new government warning (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Maria Jose Latorre\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Aug 18 (Reuters) - Chile's peso and the Brazilian real broke through key levels on Wednesday, putting pressure on the countries' central banks to follow through on threats to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <CLP=CL><CLP=> broke through the 500 peso-per-dollar level for the first time since January.\par \par \uc2 The region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were boosted by strong demand for a German government bond auction, increasing demand for some higher-risk assets.\par \par \uc2 Concerns over U.S. economic growth, which are expected to keep returns on U.S. Treasuries near record lows, have also prompted investors to pour money into Latin America's higher-yielding debt, lifting the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the sharp rise in Chile's peso prompted the government to issue another warning to the market Wednesday, saying it is closely monitoring the peso's appreciation and wants a competitive exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 After firming to 498.20 per dollar, the peso pared gains but still traded 0.1 percent stronger at 501.60 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The market has already factored in strong growth for the country, and is foreseeing further interest rate hikes, which in turn strengthens the peso," one trader in Santiago said.\par \par \uc2 Chile's GDP expanded 4.3 percent in the second quarter compared with the first quarter, data Wednesday showed, the fastest pace since at least the mid-1990s. For details, see [ID:nN18182427]\par \par \uc2 Chile's economy has recovered much faster than expected from the effects of a devastating earthquake in February, boosting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to seven-month highs.\par \par \uc2 The government might decide to slow its repatriation of dollars from copper revenues as a way to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, analysts said. [ID:nN17124678]\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL'S REAL BACKS OFF\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> also firmed past the psychologically important level of 1.75 real-per-dollar but struggled to remain there.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  toyed with the level throughout the session, and traded 0.28 percent stronger at 1.748 against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The economy is growing and rates are high, so inflows are inevitable," said Doug Smith, head of Latin American research at Standard Chartered.\par \par \uc2 "Brazil has allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to absorb a great deal of appreciation pressure, unlike the Chinese, and so have a legitimate argument that Brazil has carried much of the global appreciation pressure in the region."\par \par \uc2 If the real remains stronger than the 1.75 level for an extended period, analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act via verbal warnings, bigger or multiple dollar purchases in the spot market or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 But analysts at Brazil's Prosper brokerage said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could strengthen to 1.70 per dollar because of huge inflows, partly due to the upcoming capital-raising plan by state-run oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 "Besides this, we expect additional foreign inflows (excluding investment in \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 ) via bonds and/or shares of $5-6 billion in the short term."\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=><MEX01> closely tracked the performance of the U.S. stock market throughout the day, trading flat at 12.5990 in the afternoon session. U.S. stocks were slightly higher in afternoon trade.\par \par \uc2 The performance of U.S. assets is closely watched by investors in Mexico due to the countries' strong trade links.\par \par \uc2 Juan Carlos Lopez, head of trading at brokerage Intercam in Mexico City, said the peso would be stuck between 12.58 and 12.63 per dollar during the session due to the lack of important economic data in Mexico or the United States. (Additional reporting by Jean Luis Arce and Michael O'Boyle in Mexico City and Molly Rasbach in Santiago; editing by Jeffrey Benkoe)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100821e68i00088\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
