\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso firms, but  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk crimps\b0\par\par\uc2 704 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2010\par 17:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Strong second-quarter growth in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosts \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso pares gains after new government warning\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real firms 0.11 pct, Mexican peso slips\par \par \uc2 * Bond flows support region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  (New throughout, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Froilan Romero and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO/MEXICO CITY, Aug 18 (Reuters) - Chile's peso firmed to a seven-month high on Wednesday after stronger-than-expected growth in the second quarter raised bets the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep hiking interest rates.\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared intraday gains after the Chilean finance minister said the government wanted a competitive peso, stoking concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real and Colombia's peso were also hemmed in by the looming threat that authorities could enter \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem sharp gains that are hurting exporters.\par \par \uc2 Data showed Chile's economy expanded at the fastest pace since the mid-1990s in the second quarter from the previous quarter as the country bounces back from an earthquake earlier this year. For details, see [ID:nN18182427]\par \par \uc2 "The Chilean economy stands out in the region for having strong growth ahead of it while in other places we have begun to see moderation," said Jimena Zuniga, an analyst at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "This is consistent with a significant increase in the level of interest rates, so that combination is boosting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she added. Earlier this month Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightened borrowing costs for the third month in a row, bringing its key rate to 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 Weak U.S. growth is expected to keep yields on U.S. Treasuries near record lows for some time. That has boosted the appeal of Latin America's higher-yielding debt and lifted the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TALKING TOUGH\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso has surged almost 9 percent since the end of June. While pressure is building on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the gains, Zuniga said policymakers would not want to jeopardize their credibility.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a level that later on proves to be sustainable," she said.\par \par \uc2 The government could curb its sale of dollars from copper exports, but that would not outweigh the larger draw to local assets due to the government's reconstruction efforts that are boosting growth, analysts said. [ID:nN17124678]\par \par \uc2 Colombia's government said on Wednesday it was looking at ways to improve productivity to give businesses short-term relief from the strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has surged on inflows into the country's energy and mining sectors. [ID:nN18206932]\par \par \uc2 The Colombia peso <COP=STFX> bid 0.17 percent weaker 1,1810.60 per dollar a day after jumping by the most in three months.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to detail new efforts to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength at its policy meeting on Friday. Analysts think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could reinstate a dollar-purchase program that expired in June. [ID:nN18197601]\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> bid 0.11 percent stronger at 1.751 per U.S. dollar, touching the psychological level of 1.75 and adding to concerns that country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon step up efforts to weaken the real.\par \par \uc2 The government may test other measures before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market, said Luiz Antonio Abdo, the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at the \uc2 Souza Barros\uc2  brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "Before acting directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, it could carry out less direct measures such as offering incentives to exporters or taxing imports. As such, it would be acting in more of a fiscal way, closing the door to more speculators," Abdo said.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> lagged the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , slipping 0.25 percent to 12.63 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the peso traded a range due to a lack of U.S. data that could either ease or reinforce concerns about a slowing economy in the United States, Mexico's top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 Early in the session, the Mexican peso hit a one-week high. (Additional reporting by Samantha Pearson in Sao Paulo; Editing by Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100821e68i00087\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
