\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Colombia and  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 's pesos soar, c.banks eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2010\par 21:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Traders test out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threats across region\par \par \uc2 * Colombia's peso jumps by most in three months\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso at strongest in seven months\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real firms 0.11 pct; Mexican peso adds 0.62 pct (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Nelson Bocanegra and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA/MEXICO CITY (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened Tuesday after data suggested the U.S. economy will keep growing, while solid debt auctions in Europe supported bids for riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's peso jumped by the most in three months and Chile's peso hit a seven-month high, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Mexico and Brazil firmed to one-week highs.\par \par \uc2 A 1 percent rise in U.S. industrial output for July suggested the economy of the United States had enough strength to support economic expansion in the region. U.S. producer prices also rose last month, calming fears of deflation.\par \par \uc2 "The fact that U.S. industrial production continues to advance is good news since this is the sector behind Mexico's recovery," said Luis Flores, an economist at brokerage IXE in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's rebound last year from deep recession was fueled by manufacturing exports. Many of Mexico's factories supply U.S. plants.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso gained 0.62 percent to 12.59 per dollar, gaining ground for the fourth straight session.\par \par \uc2 The United States is also Colombia's top trading partner, and Colombia's peso bid 1.52 percent stronger at 1807.00 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is heading back toward a two-year high hit last week.\par \par \uc2 One trader in New York said that the Colombian peso had been boosted in early trading by a huge inflow from a dealer based in the city.\par \par \uc2 Also lifting demand for emerging market assets, Irish and Spanish bond auctions yielded solid results, easing concerns about Europe's debt troubles.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  LOOMS\par \par \uc2 Investors are buying Colombian bonds based on expectations that the country will soon regain its investment grade credit rating under an ambitious reform agenda set by the country's new president, Juan Manuel Santos.\par \par \uc2 Investors have flocked to Latin America's higher-yielding debt, strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , due to expectations that slow U.S. growth will keep returns on U.S. Treasuries at record lows.\par \par \uc2 But that is raising the specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the region as policy-makers look to protect exporters and prevent the formation of bubbles in the market.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real bid 0.11 percent stronger at 1.753, paring gains after hitting the psychologically important level of 1.75 reais per U.S. dollar. Analysts think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could aggressively step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if this level is broken for an extended period.\par \par \uc2 "There is a certain apprehension in the market about betting against the U.S. dollar at this level, which is lending very strong support to the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Luciano Rostagno, chief strategist for CM Capital Markets in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 One way that this level might be broken, he said, is if a mass of dollars flows into the country. Weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reports on dollar flows -- the latest of which is due on Wednesday -- have shown dollars starting to flow back into Brazil after flowing out during June and most of July.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government has also threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets last week following a rapid rise in the country's peso, but traders have continued to test the resolve of the authorities.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso was bid 0.66 percent firmer at 502.00 per dollar, hitting a fresh seven-month high. (Additional reporting by Samantha Pearson and Silvio Cascione in Sao Paulo, Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City; editing by Todd Eastham)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|FUN    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100820e68h001fe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
