\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Chile president warns will keep peso competitive\b0\par\par\uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2010\par 18:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Pinera says to use every tool to keep peso competitive\par \par \uc2 * Taming peso a challenge-analysts\par \par \uc2 * Peru gov't moves to ease sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Updates with peso close, adds analyst quote)\par \par \uc2 By Antonio de la Jara and Brad Haynes\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Aug 12 (Reuters) - Chilean President Sebastian Pinera said on Thursday he was worried about the recent sharp appreciation of the country's peso <CLP=CL> \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and warned his government would use all macroeconomic tools to keep it competitive.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso closed on Thursday at a new 5-month high versus the U.S. dollar of 509.50. Even though the peso has depreciated 0.5 percent against the dollar so far this year, in recent weeks it has seen sharp gains from strength in global bourses, higher prices for the country's main export of copper and expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to raise rates.\par \par \uc2 The peso approached 7-month intraday highs before Pinera spoke but later eased.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciates toward the 470/480 level. Neighboring Peru is also seeking to tame its sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <PEN=PE> as its economy surges, while Colombia's peso is at two-year highs. For more, see [ID:nN12111152] [ID:nN12112796]\par \par \uc2 "We have lots of problems and one of them is the exchange rate, which worries us," Pinera told a local radio station. "We will do everything we can with our macroeconomic policies; fiscal spending, debt policy to ensure that Chile continues to have a competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 A stronger peso adds costs to exports in the world's top copper producer, which is also a key exporter of wood pulp, fruit, salmon and wine.\par \par \uc2 TAMING PESO A CHALLENGE\par \par \uc2 Some analysts say Pinera and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have a hard time to rein in the peso as the economy rebounds from a massive Feb. 27 earthquake and from the global crisis.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to raise its benchmark rate by 50 basis points to 2 percent later on Thursday, marking a third aggressive rate increase in as many months as domestic demand remains strong. For a preview, see [ID:nN0965183]\par \par \uc2 "The problem with Chile is that they're currently hiking rates. It doesn't make too much sense to be hiking rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, a strategist at RBS Securities in Stamford, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 She added that the government's move to repatriate copper savings in dollars for post-quake reconstruction would also complicate efforts to tame the peso.\par \par \uc2 Joseph Ramos, an economist at the Universidad de \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said authorities would likely need to go beyond verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I don't think verbal warnings are enough," he said, saying the bank could opt for additional dollar purchases to boost reserves, but said the bank would be unlikely to act unless the peso appreciated to around 470 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "There are other options. One is a tax on capital inflows," Ramos added. "There are other instruments, like not selling as many dollars now to fund (post-quake) reconstruction."\par \par \uc2 Investors expect Chile's peso to hold onto gains by the year end if copper prices remain high and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to aggressively raise rates, but do not rule out swings in the interim. [ID:nN11234503]\par \par \uc2 Top financial players predict the peso will trade at 510 per dollar by year-end, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll showed on Wednesday. [ID:nN11245410]\par \par \uc2 Analysts say government plans to regulate taxation of derivatives to encourage \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging by smaller companies as part of wider capital market reforms, could add upward pressure to the peso by boosting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity, clearing uncertainty and luring investment. For more, see [ID:nN11223689] (Additional reporting by Samantha Pearson in Sao Paulo and Marco Aquino in Lima. Writing by Alonso Soto) (Editing by Simon Gardner and Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-ECONOMY/PINERA (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100812e68c001hg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
