\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-LatAm  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  post strong July gains\b0\par\par\uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2010\par 16:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chile peso posts best month in eight months\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real, Mexico peso see best month since March\par \par \uc2 * U.S. Midwest business survey eases double dip fears (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, July 30 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened on Friday after a surprisingly strong survey on business activity in the U.S. Midwest eased fears the slowing U.S. economy could fall back into recession.\par \par \uc2 Friday's gains capped the best month for Brazil's real and Mexico's peso since March, while Chile's peso surged by the most in eight months.\par \par \uc2 Solid corporate earnings reports in the region and in the United States during July helped offset concerns that the U.S. recovery is losing steam. On Friday, a report showed business activity in the U.S. Midwest grew more than expected. For details, see [ID:nN30265688]\par \par \uc2 "This data dissolved a bit the doubts about the pace of recovery," said Ramon Cordova, a trader at brokerage BASE in Monterrey, Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Mexico, whose factories operate in lockstep with its northern neighbor, saw its peso <MXN=> gain the most, firming 0.67 percent to 12.6455 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> bid 0.28 percent stronger to 1.754 per dollar in the local spot market. Gains in the real were muted by lingering concerns the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the derivatives market to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso <CLP=CL> ended 0.44 percent stronger at 521 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated 4.8 percent during the month. Traders said it was helped by expectations the government would start cashing in its copper revenues to pay debts, bringing more dollars to the market.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso gained about 2.4 percent in July and the real posted a 2.7 percent advance.\par \par \uc2 EYES ON JOBS, FACTORY DATA\par \par \uc2 U.S. second-quarter GDP growth data on Friday showed the economy is slowing, reinforcing expectations for low U.S. interest rates well into 2011. [ID:nN30215488]\par \par \uc2 But analysts said surveys on factory activity from around the world and the monthly U.S. jobs report could help set a new tone to markets next week.\par \par \uc2 "We have some critical numbers coming out that will maybe give investors higher conviction on whether the economy is heading back toward another recession or if we are due for a moderate slowdown," said Paul Biszko, senior emerging markets analyst at RBC in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 Under the latter outcome, Latin America's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should gain as investors are drawn to the region's higher yields, Biszko said.\par \par \uc2 In the Brazilian interest rate futures market, yields fell sharply <0#DIJ:> as investors reduced their expectations for further rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 As booming growth in Latin America's biggest economy has shown signs of slowing, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come under less pressure to contain inflation by raising of borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday released broadly dovish minutes from last week's rate-setting meeting, prompting investors to bet the tightening cycle was coming to an end. [ID:nN29199648]\par \par \uc2 The yield on the contract due January 2011 <DIJF1>, which has slumped 61 basis points since June 30, fell to 10.77 percent from 10.82 percent.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100802e67u001a6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
