\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Currency Intervention \highlight\uc2  An Unlikely Threat-For Now\b0\par\par\uc2 1,003 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2010\par 17:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1502 GMT [Dow Jones] Chilean officials have over the past year suggested the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to contain the peso's appreciation. At current levels, Flavia Cattan-Naslausky of RBS says, "the peso is fairly valued against 5-year averages and with the normalization of inflation." But that doesn't mean the possibility is gone. "[In] the same way that inflation in Chile is volatile and tends to over/undershoot, we see the same sharp moves in the REER rate before it stabilizes," she said. Therefore, RBS is adjusting its Chile position in the non-deliverable forwards market "to ensure profits." (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1501 GMT [Dow Jones] Long-term Treasury futures prices in very tight ranges, facing conflicting forces: $21B 10-yr cash note auction and expectations this afternoon's Fed speak will reiterate FOMC minutes released Tues -- that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intends to maintain its extremely accommodative policies for quite some time. Technically, Jun 30-yr Tsy bonds turned higher after touching Tues' low of 114-11. Recently at 114-16, up 3/32. Jun 10-yr Tsy notes recently up 4/32 at 115-11. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1456 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds cling on to the day's gains as continuing worries over Greek finances support safe haven assets. The market remains concerned that Greece may want to renegotiate the terms of the EU/IMF aid deal, especially with the government revising up its fiscal deficit for 2009 and an impending USD10 billion government bond sale marketed as an emerging market asset. Today's data included March euro zone services PMI (54.1 vs 53.7 forecast), PPI rose 0.1% on month in February, 4Q GDP was revised to flat over 3Q vs 0.1% rise previously. Germany sold EUR6Bln Schatz 1% March 2012, EUR2Bln OBLei 2.25% 2013. The bund yield curve marginally flattens, with the 2-year/10-year benchmark spread tightening to +216.4bps from +217.4bps. The June bund futures contract is currently up 0.21 at 123.15, within an 122.83-123.32 range . The 10-year benchmark bund is up 0.23 at 101.07, yielding 3.121%, within 3.093%-3.154% range. (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1453 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  is "warming up" to "finally" get bullish on Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There has been broad market support for the lira, but Goldman was scared the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hike rates too late. Now, though, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has signaled a more hawkish attitude, leading Goldman to expect measures to reduce market liquidity this month and higher rates soon after. "We are looking for opportunities to enter long TRY positions vs EUR and USD," analysts said in a note, which adds TRY could outperform the Brazilian real. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1431 GMT [Dow Jones] The Province of Ontario (Aa1/AA-) launched its $2B 10-year bond due April 14, 2020 at m/s+52 bps, directly in line with preliminary price guidance. BofAML/Deutsche/JPM/RBC are joint lead managers for the offering which is expected to settle on April 14.\par \par \uc2 (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1430 GMT [Dow Jones] The \uc2 Royal Bank Of Canada\uc2  sold its $1.5 billion covered bond deal to strong investor demand, and at price of 45 bps over Tsy yields. The five-year issue drew about $1.75 billion in demand from investors, according to sources familiar with the deal. (prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1427 GMT [Dow Jones] Global Geophysical Services will sell $200M in 7-year notes to refinance its existing debt. \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 , B of A and \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  are taking the deal on a roadshow starting tomorrow. The notes are noncallable for four years and include an equity clawback provision.\par \par \uc2 katherine.greene@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 1423 GMT [Dow Jones] There's good buying and selling of agency mortgages, in a sign that this market is taking steps to stand on its own after the end of the Federal Reserve's support program. Risk premiums are unchanged at 130 bps over Tsy yields. (prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1416 GMT [Dow Jones] The Conference Board's CEO confidence index, which had increased to 64 in 4Q of 2009, fell back to 62 in 1Q of 2010. The board said CEOs rated current economic and industry conditions favorably, but they worried the pace of growth will not pick up in the months ahead. Even so, more than 30% of CEOs anticipate an increase in employment levels in their industry, up significantly from less than 3% a year ago. (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1414 GMT [Dow Jones] The municipal bond market feels a little soft, with prices likely unchanged to off by about 1 or 2 bps, according to \uc2 Eaton Vance\uc2 's Evan Rourke. While "there's clearly individual interest" for munis, dealers seem to be grappling with an inventory overhang. (RV)\par \par \uc2 1406 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CAD dipped to the 0.9995 area after news that the Ivey PMI was stronger than expected at 57.8 in Mar, but has since rebounded to 1.0007. In recent trading USD has remains above earlier session low of 0.9979, according to EBS via CQG. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1345 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish Treasury bonds are slightly weaker as risk aversion rises on new worries over Greece's debt situation, also in line with a slightly weaker zloty, traders say. Average yield on 2-year paper is at 4.53% versus 4.51% late Tuesday, on 5-year at 5.17% vs 5.14%, on 10-year at 5.59% vs 5.56%. EUR/PLN trades at 3.8365 from 3.8327 earlier Wednesday, USD/PLN at 2.8733 from 2.8631. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com) [ 04-07-10 1103ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100407e6470009t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
