\par\par \b \uc2 Chile stocks, peso tumble on global bourse rout\b0\par\par\uc2 638 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2010\par 18:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Stocks close 2 pct lower, in line with global bourses\par \par \uc2 * Global bourses drag Chilean stocks off life highs\par \par \uc2 * Peso falls 1 pct to new 14-week low (Updates with bourse close, adds fresh quote, background)\par \par \uc2 By Aaron Nelsen and Maria Jose Latorre\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Feb 4 (Reuters) - Chile's blue chip IPSA index <.IPSA> tumbled 2 percent on Thursday and the peso fell to a fresh 14-week low, tracking a rout on global bourses on fears of sovereign debt problems in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Global bourses fell sharply, with Brazil's Bovespa <.BVSP> down 4.73 percent and the Dow Jones industrial average <.DJI> down 2.4 percent. [ID:nN04194705]\par \par \uc2 The IPSA closed 2 percent lower at 3,774.20 points, but ended off the day's lows, retreating from a new life closing high of 3,853.58 set on Tuesday. The all-market IGPA <.IGPA> fell 1.62 percent to 17,499.33 points.\par \par \uc2 Sovereign debt "risks in Spain, Portugal and Greece, dragged European stocks lower and infected world markets. There was also negative employment data in the United States. Both caused Chile's bourse to fall," said Francisco Hazbun, a trader with Tanner brokerage in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 "There was also some profit-taking," he added.\par \par \uc2 Shares of industrial conglomerate Copec fell 2.06 percent to 8,200 pesos per share, while rival forestry group CMPC closed 2.53 percent lower at 22,150 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Shares of Soquimich , Chile's leading exporter of fertilizer and the world's biggest producer of iodine and lithium, tumbled 3.1 percent to 19,500 pesos per share, while shares of Chile's leading electricity generator, \uc2 Endesa\uc2  , ended 1.59 percent lower at 910 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Regional airline LAN fell 1.52 percent to 8,760.1 pesos. President-elect Sebastian Pinera is set to sell his major stake worth around $1.5 billion on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The IPSA is still trading about 5.4 percent higher year-to-date and is seen ending 2010 around 15 percent higher.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day Chile's peso <CLP=CL> closed 1 percent lower to a new 14-week low, extending a sharp sell-off a day earlier on wider dollar strength and global stock losses.\par \par \uc2 The peso fell to 543.50/544.00 per U.S. dollar compared with Wednesday's close of 538.00/538.50, but ended off the day's lows. The peso is now down 6.7 percent against the dollar year-to-date.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank as much as 2 percent on Wednesday due to bank dollar buying related to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity measure.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said ongoing uncertainty spawned by modifications to rules governing pension fund hedging was also weighing on the peso, but said the market was overreacting.\par \par \uc2 "We are witnessing the effects of the changes in norms regarding pension fund hedging, which is having an impact that goes beyond their implications," the BCI brokerage said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 "Reallocations in pension fund portfolios means that they are not renewing forward sales contracts, which are pressuring the exchange rate," it added. "We should see worry at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the transitory impact of this rise (in the dollar) given it could hit inflationary expectations."\par \par \uc2 Christian Vidal, director of FXCM \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , does not expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the peso depreciates to around 600 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, analysts said banks snapped up dollars to prepare for a Feb. 8 expiry of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure that allowed banks to use pesos instead of dollars for reserve requirements on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits.\par \par \uc2 Market losses on Wednesday deepened when technical stop loss levels were triggered. (Editing by Simon Gardner and Diane Craft)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHILE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100204e624001os\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
