\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS- \highlight22\uc2 Chile central bank \highlight\uc2  may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in peso rally\b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2009\par 18:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen if 30 percent rally continues\par \par \uc2 * Any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen slowing rally, not stopping it\par \par \uc2 * Dollar abroad, copper prices to determine direction\par \par \uc2 By Maria Jose Latorre\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Nov 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may make good on threats to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb a peso rally of around 30 percent against the dollar if it continues much longer, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso has been one of the best performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar this year, rallying to 16-month highs despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's warnings about a rapid appreciation so far this year that is hurting exporters.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed flat on Friday at 493.00/493.50 per dollar, clawing back after tumbling to around 500 pesos per dollar in early trade as investors cut risk exposure on Dubai debt woes and pile into the dollar.\par \par \uc2 But the peso has steadily advanced in recent months, and some analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could opt to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it hits 480 per dollar, while others think the bank could wait until it hits 450 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The local market expects any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be similar to that of 2008 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  built up reserves through a dollar purchase program after the peso rose to 430 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The peso ultimately closed 2008 down 22.3 percent against the dollar, battered by global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 "(\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) might be seen sooner rather than later due to continued peso strength over the past several sessions," said Alfredo Coutino, Latin America director for \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Economy.com.\par \par \uc2 The peso has gained in the wake of wider dollar weakness against other global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gains in prices for Chile's No. 1 export, copper, and as investors who borrowed pesos at low interest rates to buy dollars to invest in Brazil closed positions.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio has said \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's free-floating system allows for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in extreme cases and has warned the bank has not ruled out doing so in future.\par \par \uc2 "Central banks usually issue a verbal warning first," said Alejandro Puente, head economist with Banco BBVA Chile. "So it's possible it could move to the next phase and eventually decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."\par \par \uc2 SWIMMING AGAINST THE TIDE?\par \par \uc2 However, analysts say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may only give short-term relief given the dollar's wider depreciation and rising copper prices. Chile's peso tends to gain in tandem with prices of copper, which have rebounded sharply from a slump during global crisis.\par \par \uc2 "You have to see where the peso is headed compared with what's happening to copper prices and what's happening to the dollar internationally," said Alberto Ramos, senior economist with \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "What the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has done in the past is simply to announce a dollar purchase program, something very transparent and characteristic of this \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keeping a close eye on the sharp appreciation of the peso and its inflationary implications, according to minutes of the bank's November monetary policy meeting published on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "You can't go thinking the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can change the trend. However, it can help slow an appreciation of the peso which is out of line with fundamentals," said Guillermo Pattillo, an economist at the University of Santiago.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts also wonder if the finance ministry could take measures to help sap peso strength, though Finance Minister Andres Velasco has said the government will do its part by raising the ceiling for peso debt issuance in 2010. (Writing by Aaron Nelsen; Editing by Simon Gardner and Kenneth Barry) ((aaron.nelsen@thomsonreuters.com; Tel: +562 370 4252))\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHILE/PESO (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|C|MTL    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091127e5br001q6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
