\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Chile Peso Closes Weaker On Dollar Rally Against Euro\b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2009\par 19:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (Updates with details of daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar sale.) \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Carolina Pica\f28 \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar Friday on the greenback's rally against the euro in international markets.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP501.30 to the dollar compared with CLP500.70 the previous session, after moving in a broad range of CLP500.60 to CLP507.60.\par \par \uc2 The dollar held on to its gains against the euro and other higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday morning as revived concerns about how fast the global economy will rebound prompted investors to shun riskier assets. The peso often moves in the same direction the euro does against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Losses in U.S. stock markets and lower London copper prices also contributed to the peso's tumble, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the week, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been trading at 16-month highs against the dollar, but the dollar's recent gains and comments from the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the bank couldn't rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market pulled the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below the CLP500-mark.\par \par \uc2 The peso is trading about 22% stronger against the dollar from where it began the year, fueling exporters and farmers to ask for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Exporters say their products are losing competitiveness abroad, while farmers say they'll lose money this season on the stronger peso.\par \par \uc2 In its daily sales on behalf of the Finance Ministry, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $40 million at a weighted average of CLP506.16 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't provide information on which banks bid for dollar sales.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the year, the Finance Ministry began a $4 billion sale, repatriated from one of its sovereign-wealth funds, in the local market. The ministry is selling the $4 billion to finance this year's expected fiscal deficit, at a rate of $40 million a day.\par \par \uc2 Friday's dollar sale was the last one scheduled as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  today completed the sale of the $4 billion.\par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, yields on the inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended unchanged in a session with thin, interbank transactions, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Yields on Chilean five-year BCUs ended at 2.65%, unchanged from Thursday. The yield on 10-year BCUs ended at 3.17%, also unchanged from the previous session.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-820-4244; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 20-11-09 1833GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091120e5bk0016w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
