\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Chilean  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Doesn't Rule Out  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2009\par 18:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't rule out more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso has been trading at a 16-month high against the U.S. dollar, prompting exporters to call for market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their products lose competitiveness abroad.\par \par \uc2 Higher international copper prices and the euro's gains against the dollar have been contributing forces in the peso's gains.\par \par \uc2 In prepared remarks at a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conference, De Gregorio said the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April 2008 when the exchange rate was "over appreciated" and "strengthening international liquidity by way of accumulating reserves made sense."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspended in September 2008 because of the lack of liquidity in the market caused by the international financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 "In the future, we won't rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again," De Gregorio said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reacted to the central banker's comments, and to the dollar's gains against the euro on international markets, and closed 1.6% weaker from the previous session.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-820-4241; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 19, 2009 12:09 ET (17:09 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020091119e5bj005jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
