\par\par \b \uc2 Chile peso falls sharply on firm dlr, weak copper\b0\par\par\uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2009\par 18:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Traders cite technical correction after peso rally\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President again warns of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Nov 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso <CLP=> slid over 1.6 percent on Thursday, easing on broad-based dollar strength, global stock losses and lower prices for copper, the country's No.1 export, but was unfazed by a fresh threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 The peso, which on Wednesday flirted with 17-month highs, fell 1.64 percent to end at 500.70/501.20 per dollar compared with the previous session's close of 492.50/493.00.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the fall was largely due to profit-taking by banks after recent sharp gains took the peso's year-to-date appreciation against the dollar to as much as 30 percent.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the fall was not influenced by weakness in the real after Brazil's government late on Wednesday announced a new 1.5 percent tax when overseas investors convert U.S.-listed American Depositary Receipts of Brazilian companies into local shares.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's move prompted some other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall as investors worried about the introduction of capital controls to stem speculative flows. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in India and Indonesia came under pressure in the wake of Brazil's move.\par \par \uc2 Russia's ruble, meanwhile, weakened after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up rhetoric against speculative bets on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a long rally fueled by oil prices, while South Korea's financial watchdog introduced liquidity control measures.\par \par \uc2 "Markets abroad are very negative. This is the (dollar) bounce that the market was expecting," said Rodrigo Sarria, a traders with the Celfin Capital brokerage.\par \par \uc2 "The kind of fall (the dollar has) seen generates this kind of bounce, but it is not a change in trend, and if external markets or commodities continue (to gain), we will again see the peso trading at levels we've seen this week of around 490 per dollar," he added.\par \par \uc2 The market had already priced in threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio said on Thursday the bank had not ruled out "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the future," repeating a warning he made last week.\par \par \uc2 "This is the typical kind of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the market had been expecting," Sarria added. "De Gregorio says he could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at some point ... but I don't think the market is nervous about that."\par \par \uc2 The peso has been one of the best-performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year against a weaker U.S. dollar, and is trading around 16-month highs. Some analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it hits 480 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 /PESO (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091119e5bj001cx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
