\par\par \b \uc2 Chile peso rallies past 500/dlr, nears 16-mo high\b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2009\par 12:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chile peso breaks 500/dlr psychological barrier\par \par \uc2 * Firm copper prices, end of carry trades boost peso\par \par \uc2 * Gov't again warns to keep close eye on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank seen heightening warnings before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Froilan Romero\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Nov 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso <CLP=CL> rose to a near 16-month high on Monday, breaking the psychological 500 per dollar level on carry trade closures and higher copper prices, despite warnings of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The peso firmed 1.1 percent to close at 496.30/496.80 per dollar, slightly off the day's highs. The peso closed at 501.80/502.10 per U.S. dollar on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Andres Velasco on Monday again signaled that the government was keeping a close eye on the country's peso after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem a sharp appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The government is closely watching the exchange rate," Velasco said, repeating a warning he had made on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Last week, we took measures during the passage of the budget, when we practically doubled the ceiling for debt issuance so the next government has an alternative and can avoid selling dollars and instead issue peso bonds if it wishes," he added.\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  senior economist, Alberto Ramos, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely refrain from an outright \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keep warning the market if the peso keeps gaining ground.\par \par \uc2 "It is still too early to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Certainly you can see some verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the appreciation is still a recent phenomenon, and it's not disassociated from a global weak dollar," Ramos said.\par \par \uc2 "They will probably wait until the peso crosses 475 or 450 (per dollar), in territory were the overvaluation is very clear."\par \par \uc2 He said the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could entail direct purchases of U.S. dollar in the market.\par \par \uc2 FIRM COPPER BOOSTS PESO\par \par \uc2 Traders said the peso was propelled by firm prices for No.1 export copper, which hit its highest level in more than 13 months on the London Metal Exchange on Monday <MCU3> at around $6,830 a tonne, boosted by a weak dollar, and bad weather in major metals consumer China and improving Japanese growth data.\par \par \uc2 "The fundamentals are very positive. Copper prices are at new highs in London and the markets have firmed significantly," said one trader, asking not to be named.\par \par \uc2 "At a local level, we continue to see inflows of dollars as investors end carry trades," he added.\par \par \uc2 Until recently, many carry trade investors borrowed in Chilean pesos at low interest rates and used the proceeds to buy dollars on the Chilean market to invest in Brazil, where rates are higher.\par \par \uc2 In closing these trades, the investors must buy Chilean pesos to repay those peso-denominated loans.\par \par \uc2 Copper is Chile's No.1 export and strong copper prices tend to underpin the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders said a 24 percent rise in Chile's copper export revenues to $2.48 billion in October compared with $2.0 billion in the same month a year ago, also helped buoy the peso.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained around 28 percent so far this year, making it one of the world's best-performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (With reporting by Maria Jose Latorre. Writing by Alonso Soto, Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|MNI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091116e5bg0017n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
