\par\par \b \uc2 LATIN AMERICAN MARKETS: Brazil Stocks Drop; Chile Rate Decision On Tap\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carla Mozee  \par \uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2009\par 01:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 A broad-based sell-off hit Brazilian equities Thursday, with investors taking gains from a three-session winning streak off the table as a downturn in prices for resources pressured commodity-related heavyweights.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's Bovespa equity index fell 3% to 64,447.93 as shares in consumer staple companies, home builders, telecommunication-services provider and miners were the worst performers of the session.\par \par \uc2 Meatpacker JBS (JBSAY) dropped 6.5% and air carrier TAM (TAM) fell 6%, pacing decliners.\par \par \uc2 Mining giant Vale (RIO) shares dropped 4.1%, Gerdau (GGB) fell 4.3% and MMX Mineracao lost 4.7%. The steel producer reported a third-quarter net loss of 27.2 million reals, narrower than its loss in the year-ago period.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  (PBR), the most heavily weighted on the Bovespa index, slumped 2% as crude-oil futures slid 3% to below $76.94 a barrel. Crude prices fell after U.S. government data showed weak demand and higher inventories.\par \par \uc2 Separately, \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 ' third-quarter results are due late Friday.\par \par \uc2 Prices for crude, as well as for silver, copper and platinum, were also pressured on Thursday because of rise in the U.S. dollar against its key rivals. The greenback found support after U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner said the government's borrowing needs would be less than it had anticipated. The dollar index (DXY) rose 0.6%.\par \par \uc2 But back in Sao Paulo, shares of \uc2 Lojas Renner\uc2  climbed 2.3% after MSCI Barra said the department-store operator will be added to its MSCI Emerging Markets Index.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Banco do Brasil\uc2  were one of the few advancers on Thursday, rising 0.2% after the state-run bank said third-quarter earnings rose 6%.\par \par \uc2 In Santiago, Chile's IPSA fell 0.9% ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision on interest rates. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to hold its key rate at the ultra-low level of 0.5%.\par \par \uc2 The key issue for investors will be what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do with its liquidity facility, according to RBS Securities. Policymakers in late October outlined gradual phasing of 28-day repo \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with flexible collateral and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The strength of the [Chilean peso] has triggered some rumors that the [\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] will not only phase out the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps quickly but that it could even start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to curb the appreciating trend," wrote RBS Securities economist Benito Berber in a note to clients Thursday.\par \par \uc2 According to media reports Wednesday, Jose de Gregorio, the president of Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the bank is considering a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at cooling the peso's rise.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso recently reached a 15-month high against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 MSCI bulks up Brazil's index presence\par \par \uc2 Index provider MSCI Barra late Wednesday, as part of its semiannual review, said that 11 Brazilian companies will be added to its MSCI Emerging Markets Index. The additions are the most for one country, followed by China, which will see seven issues added and one deleted. The index tracks issues from 22\par \par \uc2 Brazil's PDG Realty and \uc2 Lojas Renner\uc2  will be the largest additions to the index. The changes will be in effect as of the close of Nov. 30.\par \par \uc2 The heftier representation of Brazilian companies on the index arrives as Brazil's Bovespa has surged 72% this year as investors seek exposure to Latin America's largest economy. The country was the first in the region to emerge out of recession.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, Brazil has been working to curb a surge in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and "can only see its challenges exacerbated by the MSCI decision," in part because not all of the new companies being added to the EM index have U.S.-listed shares or dual listings, said Marc Chandler, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 , in a note to clients Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian officials have reportedly been considering extending measures to pull back the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. Last month, Brazil levied a 2% tax on all foreign purchases of stocks and fixed-income assets.\par \par \uc2 More than $3 trillion are benchmarked against its indexes worldwide, estimates MSCI. [ 11-12-09 1915ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020091113e5bd00002\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
