\par\par \b \uc2 Chile finmin says keeping close eye on strong peso\b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2009\par 18:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Nov 12 (Reuters) - Chilean Finance Minister Andres Velasco said on Thursday he was keeping a close eye on the country's peso after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem a sharp appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president said it yesterday and I have said it many times and I repeat: We never sit with our arms crossed on this topic," Velasco said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio late on Tuesday said \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's free-float system "leaves us room to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in extreme circumstances."\par \par \uc2 Velasco said a Senate decision to raise the ceiling for government peso debt issuance for 2010 to $7 billion from $3.5 billion previously would help peso competitiveness by enabling the government to avoid repatriating dollars held abroad and selling them on the local market.\par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=CL> has been one of the world's best-performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year against a weakening U.S. dollar, rising around 26 percent year-to-date.\par \par \uc2 It rallied further after Brazil in October introduced a tax on capital inflows, prompting the accelerated closing of carry trades in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 But the strong peso is hurting Chile's exporters and analysts believe authorities may take measures to curb its appreciation if it firms much beyond 500 pesos per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through a dollar purchase program to build up its reserves, after the peso firmed to 430 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's options included so-called sterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whereby the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars and issues bonds to absorb the extra peso liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Another option could be for a non-sterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whereby the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars to inject peso liquidity while unwinding credit facilities at a stepped-up rate to mitigate the affects of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/PESO|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091112e5bc001y0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
