\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk Pres Doesn't Rule Out  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  Peso Market\b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2009\par 19:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the peso market if the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to show a significant fluctuation, the bank's president told a group of manufacturing sector exporters Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Chile, whose economy is largely dependent on commodity-related and other types of exports, has seen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firm around 15% so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Exporters blame the Finance Ministry's decision to repatriate a total of $7 billion from one of its sovereign wealth funds.\par \par \uc2 Chile switched to a free-floating exchange rate from a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -set trading band in the late 1990s, a change which the central banker praised.\par \par \uc2 "All of the financial crises since the 1960s have all been linked to the defense of the peso," bank president Jose De Gregorio told exporters linked to the Asexma trade group.\par \par \uc2 He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in light of unusual market circumstances.\par \par \uc2 In 2008, when the peso strengthened to 10-year highs against the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took market-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, including daily dollar sales on the local market.\par \par \uc2 "Last year we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because we saw that the peso was affecting [the economy] at the aggregate level," De Gregorio said.\par \par \uc2 With regards to gross domestic product growth, De Gregorio reiterated previous comments that the economy will likely recover in the second half of the year.\par \par \uc2 Third-quarter GDP results will likely be worse than the same quarter last year, but will likely be up from the second quarter of this year, he said.\par \par \uc2 "Market expectations show an outlook for increased dynamism in the second half of the year," he said in prepared remarks.\par \par \uc2 First-quarter GDP fell 2.1% on the year. Second-quarter GDP will likely contract about 4%, according to preliminary data. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release second-quarter GDP data in August.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-820-4244; carolina.pica@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 29, 2009 13:06 ET (17:06 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090729e57t005gr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
