\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Banking Regulator: Financial System Liquidity Normal\b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2008\par 16:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Liquidity in Chile's financial system is at normal levels, and the system "is functioning with normal parameters," Chile's SBIF banking regulator said Friday.\par \par \uc2 In the past two weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has adopted several measures to maintain dollar liquidity in the local market. In addition, the Finance Ministry placed a total $1 billion in local dollar-denominated certificates of deposit, which also eased greenback liquidity.\par \par \uc2 "Banking institutions have sufficient liquidity both in local and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the SBIF said in a statement, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Finance Ministry moves helped with dollar liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The regulator said that Chile's financial system is obviously a part of the globalized economy and that it's still part of international economic cycles.\par \par \uc2 "We can affirm, however, that the fundamentals that support our banking industry allow us to calmly observe its capacity to resist the negative moments of the cycle," the regulator said.\par \par \uc2 The SBIF will continue to closely monitor any international events or moves for their repercussions on the local system, it said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say Chile's banks are on more solid ground than banks in other countries as banking regulation was tightened after a banking crisis in the 1980s, when several failing banks were \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still holds a small stake in \uc2 Banco de Chile\uc2  (BCH), the country's second-largest bank in terms of loans, as part of the 1980s bailout.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-820-4244; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 10-10-08 1437GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081010e4aa000ql\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
